(2307594, 317873, 47117, '<td valign="top">I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry in this challenge.<br/> <br/>This reminds me a bit of Bresson''s photos he took in Paris. Nice dark tones, good usage of surrounding buildings, sky, etc. The only thing is, the shot has no real candid value by way of emotion or wow factor. There is nothing happening but a good overall shot of a town.  People just walking down the road really tells me no story and has no kick to it "as a candid".  In a b/w challenge, I would score it higher, but as a candid, I gave it a 5.</td>', 'I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry in this challenge. This reminds me a bit of Bresson''s photos he took in Paris. Nice dark tones, good usage of surrounding buildings, sky, etc. The only thing is, the shot has no real candid value by way of emotion or wow factor. There is nothing happening but a good overall shot of a town.  People just walking down the road really tells me no story and has no kick to it "as a candid".  In a b/w challenge, I would score it higher, but as a candid, I gave it a 5.', '2006-04-12 16:30:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(2307598, 319919, 47117, '<td valign="top">I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry in this challenge.<br/> <br/>Children are way too easy and prime targets for candids. No one need step out of a comfort zone to get them and could get a million shots of them a day. This one is good. It does have good tones and is cute. It is out of focus though, and to me would fair better in a b/w challenge then as a candid. For me, its a 4 vote.  More focus on the face and less on the hands would have been better.</td>', 'I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry in this challenge. Children are way too easy and prime targets for candids. No one need step out of a comfort zone to get them and could get a million shots of them a day. This one is good. It does have good tones and is cute. It is out of focus though, and to me would fair better in a b/w challenge then as a candid. For me, its a 4 vote.  More focus on the face and less on the hands would have been better.', '2006-04-12 16:33:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(2307605, 319869, 47117, '<td valign="top">I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry in this challenge.<br/> <br/>This is ok, but no real wow factor for me. Just kids sitting around with a duck. Not a really big story teller, but it has some good qualities. The smallest child does exude some emotion, yet it is covered in darkness by shadows. The saturation is good on the greens.  It''s just ok for me. A 4 vote.</td>', 'I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry in this challenge. This is ok, but no real wow factor for me. Just kids sitting around with a duck. Not a really big story teller, but it has some good qualities. The smallest child does exude some emotion, yet it is covered in darkness by shadows. The saturation is good on the greens.  It''s just ok for me. A 4 vote.', '2006-04-12 16:34:39.000000', NULL, 1),
