(2307860, 319701, 47117, '<td valign="top">I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry in this challenge.<br/> <br/>This is just ok to me. I like the colors, but I find little interest in the actual candid itself. I just can''t quite grasp the corrulation between the subject and the wall, and that leaves me with little for any kind of wow factor or shall I say, kick, to the photo. It''s a 3 for me.</td>', 'I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry in this challenge. This is just ok to me. I like the colors, but I find little interest in the actual candid itself. I just can''t quite grasp the corrulation between the subject and the wall, and that leaves me with little for any kind of wow factor or shall I say, kick, to the photo. It''s a 3 for me.', '2006-04-12 18:13:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(2307862, 319856, 47117, '<td valign="top">I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry in this challenge.<br/> <br/>This is just ok for me. Not really much for this one myself. I can see he is playing the instrument, which is nice, but I guess its the colors or tones. I am just not getting a candid feel from this shot. It''s a 4 for me.</td>', 'I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry in this challenge. This is just ok for me. Not really much for this one myself. I can see he is playing the instrument, which is nice, but I guess its the colors or tones. I am just not getting a candid feel from this shot. It''s a 4 for me.', '2006-04-12 18:13:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(2307863, 319374, 55908, '<td valign="top">Interesting take on the challenge. Nice photo.</td>', 'Interesting take on the challenge. Nice photo.', '2006-04-12 18:13:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(2307864, 318802, 7322, '<td valign="top">I think the idea that the title suggest would be illustrated better if you had included a view of older skaters. The incongruity of sizes is cute but without being let in what they are looking at off-camera, my interest wanes. I think for this shot, at least one of the boys should be looking more toward the viewer.</td>', 'I think the idea that the title suggest would be illustrated better if you had included a view of older skaters. The incongruity of sizes is cute but without being let in what they are looking at off-camera, my interest wanes. I think for this shot, at least one of the boys should be looking more toward the viewer.', '2006-04-12 18:13:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(2307865, 318922, 47117, '<td valign="top">I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry in this challenge.<br/> <br/>This is ok. Wish I could kick like that. LOL...But, in these types of situations it is more performance in category to me then a candid. Although it is a candid, it is just not that unexpected or a capture of a moody type moment from someone unawares. That is what I particularly look for. So my score of a 4 is based on technicals only.</td>', 'I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry in this challenge. This is ok. Wish I could kick like that. LOL...But, in these types of situations it is more performance in category to me then a candid. Although it is a candid, it is just not that unexpected or a capture of a moody type moment from someone unawares. That is what I particularly look for. So my score of a 4 is based on technicals only.', '2006-04-12 18:14:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(2307868, 319746, 47117, '<td valign="top">I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry in this challenge.<br/> <br/>I find little interest here I''m afraid. I do like the tones, but it''s just not that interesting. It''s a 3 for me.</td>', 'I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry in this challenge. I find little interest here I''m afraid. I do like the tones, but it''s just not that interesting. It''s a 3 for me.', '2006-04-12 18:15:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(2307870, 319684, 47117, '<td valign="top">I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry in this challenge.<br/> <br/>Children are sweet. They are also the most easiest targets for candids, and I would have loved to see something a bit more out of the comfort zone for this challenge in a candid then that of a child on a slide. She is darling though, but as a candid, in my opinion, it is a 4 photo.</td>', 'I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry in this challenge. Children are sweet. They are also the most easiest targets for candids, and I would have loved to see something a bit more out of the comfort zone for this challenge in a candid then that of a child on a slide. She is darling though, but as a candid, in my opinion, it is a 4 photo.', '2006-04-12 18:16:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(2307875, 319183, 49773, '<td valign="top">Great dof and focus!</td>', 'Great dof and focus!', '2006-04-12 18:18:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(2307876, 320002, 47117, '<td valign="top">I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry in this challenge.<br/> <br/>This is alright, but I don''t see much by way of any particular interest. In categories I would list it myself as a water or an action, and not a candid.  There is really no emotional value being portrayed from any one or more persons, and just two boats with two sailors on them. I can see there is some conflict happening between the boats, but there doesn''t seem to be much concern over it that I can see.  To me, as a candid, it is a 4.</td>', 'I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry in this challenge. This is alright, but I don''t see much by way of any particular interest. In categories I would list it myself as a water or an action, and not a candid.  There is really no emotional value being portrayed from any one or more persons, and just two boats with two sailors on them. I can see there is some conflict happening between the boats, but there doesn''t seem to be much concern over it that I can see.  To me, as a candid, it is a 4.', '2006-04-12 18:18:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(2307878, 319364, 55908, '<td valign="top">Beautifully vivid!</td>', 'Beautifully vivid!', '2006-04-12 18:19:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(2307879, 319651, 47117, '<td valign="top">I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry in this challenge.<br/> <br/>This is a decent candid, but sunglasses, hats, and masks are a nightmare for a candid photographer. In this shot, sunglasses are really blocking the emotion in the faces for me. This I would list myself as more of an action shot then candid. It is a candid, but just not the type of candids I prefer to see or look for or at with any interest. It''s a 4 for me.</td>', 'I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry in this challenge. This is a decent candid, but sunglasses, hats, and masks are a nightmare for a candid photographer. In this shot, sunglasses are really blocking the emotion in the faces for me. This I would list myself as more of an action shot then candid. It is a candid, but just not the type of candids I prefer to see or look for or at with any interest. It''s a 4 for me.', '2006-04-12 18:20:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(2307882, 317515, 31628, '<td valign="top">Not only does this lack in technical and artistic appeal, I disagree with it on a moral level.  This is a terrible idea, giving wine to a toddler.</td>', 'Not only does this lack in technical and artistic appeal, I disagree with it on a moral level.  This is a terrible idea, giving wine to a toddler.', '2006-04-12 18:21:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(2307883, 319101, 7322, '<td valign="top">The title belies what the photo shows. Since this is supposed to be a candid, I don''t think it should be called eyes on the prize unless one of the dogs is actually looking at the blue ribbon in a way that appears unexpected and human.  By using selective color on the ribbon you are drawing the viewer''s attention away from the far more interesting subjects which, btw, should be doing something more interesting then looking off camera to be truly engaging. Sorry, this one just doesn''t work for me. For me, a candid needs to show something unexpected (odd juxtapositions, subject doing something out of character, e.g.) or else, reveal something about a universal theme, such as love, greed, friendship, etc. It could be argued that this reveals something about competition, but not in a way that engages my interest or provokes an emotional response in me.</td>', 'The title belies what the photo shows. Since this is supposed to be a candid, I don''t think it should be called eyes on the prize unless one of the dogs is actually looking at the blue ribbon in a way that appears unexpected and human.  By using selective color on the ribbon you are drawing the viewer''s attention away from the far more interesting subjects which, btw, should be doing something more interesting then looking off camera to be truly engaging. Sorry, this one just doesn''t work for me. For me, a candid needs to show something unexpected (odd juxtapositions, subject doing something out of character, e.g.) or else, reveal something about a universal theme, such as love, greed, friendship, etc. It could be argued that this reveals something about competition, but not in a way that engages my interest or provokes an emotional response in me.', '2006-04-12 18:21:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(2307885, 319669, 47117, '<td valign="top">I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry in this challenge.<br/> <br/>I like this shot in that without the rope, he would look like a castaway, stuck in the ocean. I almost long for that in this shot, as I think it would have given the subject of the man more interest.  However, more of the interest to me, overall, is on the ocean and the vastness of it then the subject.  To me also, the man doesn''t look relaxed, but a bit tiffed. That could just be me though. In any case, this is a 5 for me for a candid and in what I prefer to see, which are closer shots with more interest and more kick to them.</td>', 'I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry in this challenge. I like this shot in that without the rope, he would look like a castaway, stuck in the ocean. I almost long for that in this shot, as I think it would have given the subject of the man more interest.  However, more of the interest to me, overall, is on the ocean and the vastness of it then the subject.  To me also, the man doesn''t look relaxed, but a bit tiffed. That could just be me though. In any case, this is a 5 for me for a candid and in what I prefer to see, which are closer shots with more interest and more kick to them.', '2006-04-12 18:22:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(2307889, 318591, 49773, '<td valign="top">Wish there was not a tree there...</td>', 'Wish there was not a tree there...', '2006-04-12 18:24:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(2307890, 319761, 47117, '<td valign="top">I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry in this challenge.<br/> <br/>This is cute, but children are far too easy to me in order to get candids of.  This is really not anything I wouldn''t see at a park on any given day. It''s darling, but just doesn''t give me the interest I particularly care to see in a candid.  It''s a 4 photo for me.</td>', 'I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry in this challenge. This is cute, but children are far too easy to me in order to get candids of.  This is really not anything I wouldn''t see at a park on any given day. It''s darling, but just doesn''t give me the interest I particularly care to see in a candid.  It''s a 4 photo for me.', '2006-04-12 18:24:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(2307893, 319890, 7322, '<td valign="top">This is a bit too much like a snapshot for me. Very nice for the family photo album but for me, the objective viewer, there isn''t much of the unexpected happening and the children haven''t been captured in a way that evokes much of an emotional response or draws me in to their game. If this had captured some sort of expression on either of the children--triumphant win, sad defeat, or just plain silliness, it would be more successful.</td>', 'This is a bit too much like a snapshot for me. Very nice for the family photo album but for me, the objective viewer, there isn''t much of the unexpected happening and the children haven''t been captured in a way that evokes much of an emotional response or draws me in to their game. If this had captured some sort of expression on either of the children--triumphant win, sad defeat, or just plain silliness, it would be more successful.', '2006-04-12 18:26:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(2307895, 318901, 47117, '<td valign="top">I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry in this challenge.<br/> <br/>Children are far too easy to capture in a candid.  They dress in all kinds of lovely and cute attire and have no problem with the crowds and in showing their emotions in those crowds. This shot is cute in that it has the cute dress value, however, there is little else going on to give me interest.  No facial emotion, no real story, and little interest for me personally and in what I look for in a candid.  It''s a 4 photo for me.</td>', 'I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry in this challenge. Children are far too easy to capture in a candid.  They dress in all kinds of lovely and cute attire and have no problem with the crowds and in showing their emotions in those crowds. This shot is cute in that it has the cute dress value, however, there is little else going on to give me interest.  No facial emotion, no real story, and little interest for me personally and in what I look for in a candid.  It''s a 4 photo for me.', '2006-04-12 18:27:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(2307903, 318134, 47117, '<td valign="top">I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry in this challenge.<br/> <br/>This is cute. Reminds me of my grandson which is 22 hours away and it makes me miss him.  However, with that said, children are such easy candid targets.  I really would have liked to have seen a photo with a more out-of-the-comfort-zone taken, and that of a frontal view of the face so I could sense and feel the emotion.  This does, however, have interest and I do like the tones a lot. It''s a 5 from me.</td>', 'I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry in this challenge. This is cute. Reminds me of my grandson which is 22 hours away and it makes me miss him.  However, with that said, children are such easy candid targets.  I really would have liked to have seen a photo with a more out-of-the-comfort-zone taken, and that of a frontal view of the face so I could sense and feel the emotion.  This does, however, have interest and I do like the tones a lot. It''s a 5 from me.', '2006-04-12 18:30:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(2307904, 318800, 7322, '<td valign="top">This would work better if the viewer could see the expressions on the children''s faces. A rear view of a subject can be successful but there needs to be a valid creative reason for the choice. In this case, I don''t understand the choice to show their backsides. This doesn''t capture the exuberance of splashing. Also, while there are valid expections, it is generally good practice to photograph children at their eye-level.</td>', 'This would work better if the viewer could see the expressions on the children''s faces. A rear view of a subject can be successful but there needs to be a valid creative reason for the choice. In this case, I don''t understand the choice to show their backsides. This doesn''t capture the exuberance of splashing. Also, while there are valid expections, it is generally good practice to photograph children at their eye-level.', '2006-04-12 18:30:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(2307906, 319694, 47117, '<td valign="top">I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry in this challenge.<br/> <br/>Little interest here for me I''m afraid.  Just a boy reading a book is what I get from it and I find nothing that speaks to me beyond that. I do like the tones and the dof,  but as a candid and in what I like to see in them, this just doesn''t do it for me. It''s a 3 vote for me.</td>', 'I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry in this challenge. Little interest here for me I''m afraid.  Just a boy reading a book is what I get from it and I find nothing that speaks to me beyond that. I do like the tones and the dof,  but as a candid and in what I like to see in them, this just doesn''t do it for me. It''s a 3 vote for me.', '2006-04-12 18:31:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(2307914, 318800, 47117, '<td valign="top">I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry in this challenge.<br/> <br/>Children can be captured in a candid moment at any given time of the day, and from the back, side, or front, they don''t care. LOL...It isn''t really a non-comfort zone candid shot to me.  I prefer something different in a candid personally, and one that shows the face and/or more interest or has more kick to it. Something a bit more compelling. They are darling though, and it reminds me of the days when I used to splash in puddles, but for this challenge, it''s a 4 vote from me.</td>', 'I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry in this challenge. Children can be captured in a candid moment at any given time of the day, and from the back, side, or front, they don''t care. LOL...It isn''t really a non-comfort zone candid shot to me.  I prefer something different in a candid personally, and one that shows the face and/or more interest or has more kick to it. Something a bit more compelling. They are darling though, and it reminds me of the days when I used to splash in puddles, but for this challenge, it''s a 4 vote from me.', '2006-04-12 18:33:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(2307916, 317510, 7322, '<td valign="top">This is what I expect from a candid. What works is the juxtaposition of the man with crutches and the handicapped sign. The bit of painted sign on the wall gives the viewer a nice feel for the environment and adds a bit of visual interest to the backdrop as well. Nice job!</td>', 'This is what I expect from a candid. What works is the juxtaposition of the man with crutches and the handicapped sign. The bit of painted sign on the wall gives the viewer a nice feel for the environment and adds a bit of visual interest to the backdrop as well. Nice job!', '2006-04-12 18:33:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(2307929, 320045, 47117, '<td valign="top">I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry in this challenge.<br/> <br/>Nice sky, nice city, nice contrast to the grass. Looks like early morning or evening. I like the lighting, but a bit blown out on the left. However, as a candid, it holds little pizzazz and interest for me. It''s a 4 from me on this one.</td>', 'I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry in this challenge. Nice sky, nice city, nice contrast to the grass. Looks like early morning or evening. I like the lighting, but a bit blown out on the left. However, as a candid, it holds little pizzazz and interest for me. It''s a 4 from me on this one.', '2006-04-12 18:35:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(2307935, 319926, 47117, '<td valign="top">I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry in this challenge.<br/> <br/>Children are so easy to capture a candid moment from. Usually a candid shot for me, and with a child, has to exude a lot of interest or be exceptional. I like the concept of this photo. The interest of the bird and the expression does make it a good candid. Where it lacks, however, is in the technicals. I think the focus is just too far off the boy, and I so want to real that in on this shot so I can feel the moment more. It''s still a good 5 photo though. It''s a nice capture.</td>', 'I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry in this challenge. Children are so easy to capture a candid moment from. Usually a candid shot for me, and with a child, has to exude a lot of interest or be exceptional. I like the concept of this photo. The interest of the bird and the expression does make it a good candid. Where it lacks, however, is in the technicals. I think the focus is just too far off the boy, and I so want to real that in on this shot so I can feel the moment more. It''s still a good 5 photo though. It''s a nice capture.', '2006-04-12 18:38:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(2307936, 319413, 7322, '<td valign="top">I like the environment but this particular capture isn''t quite engaging me. I think what you are showing is the woman on the bike responding to the guy sleeping on the streets with his dogs. The problem for me is that I can''t really guage the woman''s emotions from this angle and I can barely see the guy with his dogs.I don''t think this really captures the moment. Ultimately, the stenciled wall is what grabs my attention in this.</td>', 'I like the environment but this particular capture isn''t quite engaging me. I think what you are showing is the woman on the bike responding to the guy sleeping on the streets with his dogs. The problem for me is that I can''t really guage the woman''s emotions from this angle and I can barely see the guy with his dogs.I don''t think this really captures the moment. Ultimately, the stenciled wall is what grabs my attention in this.', '2006-04-12 18:38:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(2307939, 319035, 7322, '<td valign="top">Without seeing what is causing the consternation in the subject''s face, it is difficult for me to be fully engaged in this. It doesn''t really tell a complete story. This seems more like one for the family photo album, IMO.</td>', 'Without seeing what is causing the consternation in the subject''s face, it is difficult for me to be fully engaged in this. It doesn''t really tell a complete story. This seems more like one for the family photo album, IMO.', '2006-04-12 18:39:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(2307940, 317625, 47117, '<td valign="top">I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry in this challenge.<br/> <br/>I don''t get the title with the photo, as I really don''t see anything sinister exuding from the boy, but I don''t vote on titles anyway. So on to the photo.  Children are far too easy to capture in candids. This one is no exception to the rule, however, they have to be exceptional in my book to qualify as a really good candid. This particular photo has good tones, but the focus is lacking quite a bit and the crop is too tight for my particular taste. It''s a 4 vote from me.</td>', 'I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry in this challenge. I don''t get the title with the photo, as I really don''t see anything sinister exuding from the boy, but I don''t vote on titles anyway. So on to the photo.  Children are far too easy to capture in candids. This one is no exception to the rule, however, they have to be exceptional in my book to qualify as a really good candid. This particular photo has good tones, but the focus is lacking quite a bit and the crop is too tight for my particular taste. It''s a 4 vote from me.', '2006-04-12 18:40:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(2307946, 319389, 47117, '<td valign="top">I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry in this challenge.<br/> <br/>Would have made a nice "hands" challenge shot, but I don''t see candid here to me. I understand the imaginative concept in that of the candid you are portraying, but to me personally, I like to see straight-on emotional moments in, preferably, the face or situation.  Here I just see that I have to imagine it rather than see it, and in that, I give this photo a 4.</td>', 'I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry in this challenge. Would have made a nice "hands" challenge shot, but I don''t see candid here to me. I understand the imaginative concept in that of the candid you are portraying, but to me personally, I like to see straight-on emotional moments in, preferably, the face or situation.  Here I just see that I have to imagine it rather than see it, and in that, I give this photo a 4.', '2006-04-12 18:42:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(2307948, 319599, 16488, '<td valign="top">This is lovely and emotive image. The colors are really striking in their complement. Grain adds a lovely nostalgia to this as well. (I do want to note for you, assuming you don''t know already, that "coolie" is an extremely offensive term in the U.S.....just in case all the low votes roll in on that account.)</td>', 'This is lovely and emotive image. The colors are really striking in their complement. Grain adds a lovely nostalgia to this as well. (I do want to note for you, assuming you don''t know already, that "coolie" is an extremely offensive term in the U.S.....just in case all the low votes roll in on that account.)', '2006-04-12 18:43:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(2307953, 320010, 47117, '<td valign="top">I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry in this challenge.<br/> <br/>This is an ok image for candid, but it is lacking in technicals. The focus fell short here and ended up closer to his feet then his face.  It does have some interest to it though, and in that I give it a 4.  I do like that he is off center and the colors on him verses the surroundings.</td>', 'I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry in this challenge. This is an ok image for candid, but it is lacking in technicals. The focus fell short here and ended up closer to his feet then his face.  It does have some interest to it though, and in that I give it a 4.  I do like that he is off center and the colors on him verses the surroundings.', '2006-04-12 18:45:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(2307957, 319988, 34133, '<td valign="top">Really good shot, probably not a good title</td>', 'Really good shot, probably not a good title', '2006-04-12 18:45:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(2307958, 318138, 7322, '<td valign="top">I don''t think this shot captures the moment that you must have witnessed because without the title, I wouldn''t have come to the conclusion that one of these children felt threatened or was being threatening. This is candid but for me, it seems to have missed the fleeting moment that would have engaged my attention in an impactful way.</td>', 'I don''t think this shot captures the moment that you must have witnessed because without the title, I wouldn''t have come to the conclusion that one of these children felt threatened or was being threatening. This is candid but for me, it seems to have missed the fleeting moment that would have engaged my attention in an impactful way.', '2006-04-12 18:47:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(2307960, 317432, 47117, '<td valign="top">I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry in this challenge.<br/> <br/>To me this is an uninteresting candid of the back of a man walking to the bus or home. I really find little "kick", if you will, and there is really no story. The title says lost in time, but I don''t get that from the photo either. It isn''t like he is dressed in period clothes or looks lost. But I don''t vote on titles anyway.  The candid itself just doesn''t do much for me I''m afraid. It''s a 3 photo to me.</td>', 'I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry in this challenge. To me this is an uninteresting candid of the back of a man walking to the bus or home. I really find little "kick", if you will, and there is really no story. The title says lost in time, but I don''t get that from the photo either. It isn''t like he is dressed in period clothes or looks lost. But I don''t vote on titles anyway.  The candid itself just doesn''t do much for me I''m afraid. It''s a 3 photo to me.', '2006-04-12 18:47:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(2307964, 319760, 34192, '<td valign="top">I really like the interaction between the two subjects.  Toning is well done, composition excellent.  Contrast a touch high, but it could be my monitor.  A good candid leaves me wanting more - the next frame.  So does this. 10</td>', 'I really like the interaction between the two subjects.  Toning is well done, composition excellent.  Contrast a touch high, but it could be my monitor.  A good candid leaves me wanting more - the next frame.  So does this. 10', '2006-04-12 18:48:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(2307966, 319608, 47117, '<td valign="top">I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry in this challenge.<br/> <br/>This is ok. I can see the emotion and like the tones, but the photo is really lacking in focus. I do like that there is more focus on the eyes then anywhere else, as most emotion is coming from them. I also like the way it is cropped. It''s just a good candid to me. I gave it a 5.</td>', 'I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry in this challenge. This is ok. I can see the emotion and like the tones, but the photo is really lacking in focus. I do like that there is more focus on the eyes then anywhere else, as most emotion is coming from them. I also like the way it is cropped. It''s just a good candid to me. I gave it a 5.', '2006-04-12 18:49:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(2307967, 318665, 7322, '<td valign="top">This reminds me of a photo in one of my vintage photography manuals. It works fairly successfully but I think I would like it better if the woman were smiling more toward the viewer.</td>', 'This reminds me of a photo in one of my vintage photography manuals. It works fairly successfully but I think I would like it better if the woman were smiling more toward the viewer.', '2006-04-12 18:49:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(2307968, 319999, 34192, '<td valign="top">This is utterly perfect.  A bunny with a chainsaw!  I like the composition - the POV, slightly up, works really well for me.  He is framed well in the doorway - his light against its dark.  Very well taken - 10.</td>', 'This is utterly perfect.  A bunny with a chainsaw!  I like the composition - the POV, slightly up, works really well for me.  He is framed well in the doorway - his light against its dark.  Very well taken - 10.', '2006-04-12 18:49:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(2307970, 319118, 49773, '<td valign="top">I would like to see how this was done without dodge/burn...???</td>', 'I would like to see how this was done without dodge/burn...???', '2006-04-12 18:50:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(2307974, 319616, 34192, '<td valign="top">Very cute kid.  I like the almost expression on his face.  I''d love to see the next few frames.  Like the slight desat - makes me focus on the subject. Very well seen. 8</td>', 'Very cute kid.  I like the almost expression on his face.  I''d love to see the next few frames.  Like the slight desat - makes me focus on the subject. Very well seen. 8', '2006-04-12 18:50:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(2307975, 319333, 47117, '<td valign="top">I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry in this challenge.<br/> <br/>This is nice. I like that you can make out the face in the piano then a straight on shot of her face, however, I would have really liked to have seen this with a tonal change to sepia or even b/w.  The contrast is giving off a green glow to me on the skintones from the shirt.  But as a candid, it is pretty. It''s not full of the interest I care to see, but its very pretty. I give it a 5.</td>', 'I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry in this challenge. This is nice. I like that you can make out the face in the piano then a straight on shot of her face, however, I would have really liked to have seen this with a tonal change to sepia or even b/w.  The contrast is giving off a green glow to me on the skintones from the shirt.  But as a candid, it is pretty. It''s not full of the interest I care to see, but its very pretty. I give it a 5.', '2006-04-12 18:51:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(2307977, 318381, 34192, '<td valign="top">Excellent timing.  Crop works even though he has no feet - it enhances the tension in this image.  His posture is perfect.  Tones well done. 9</td>', 'Excellent timing.  Crop works even though he has no feet - it enhances the tension in this image.  His posture is perfect.  Tones well done. 9', '2006-04-12 18:51:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(2307978, 319500, 47117, '<td valign="top">I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry in this challenge.<br/> <br/>This is ok. Lots of this kind of shot can be taken though, so it isn''t all that interesting to me or has any wow factors I like to look for in a candid. The tones are nice, and the intensity of her face. I give it a 5.</td>', 'I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry in this challenge. This is ok. Lots of this kind of shot can be taken though, so it isn''t all that interesting to me or has any wow factors I like to look for in a candid. The tones are nice, and the intensity of her face. I give it a 5.', '2006-04-12 18:52:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(2307982, 319992, 34192, '<td valign="top">I like these types of close-ups, though many at DPC do not.  Toning well done, crop works, POV excellent. 8</td>', 'I like these types of close-ups, though many at DPC do not.  Toning well done, crop works, POV excellent. 8', '2006-04-12 18:52:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(2307986, 319635, 34192, '<td valign="top">Wondering if he''s doing that ''cause his toupee will blow off.  That''s what great about good candids - waiting for the next frame.  Contrast a little strong for me, but could be my monitor.7</td>', 'Wondering if he''s doing that ''cause his toupee will blow off.  That''s what great about good candids - waiting for the next frame.  Contrast a little strong for me, but could be my monitor.7', '2006-04-12 18:54:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(2307987, 319417, 7322, '<td valign="top">For a candid to work it should provoke some sort of emotional response in the viewer. Generally, there is an element of the unexpected or the subject is captured revealing a strong emotion,i.e., glee, anger, frustration. This just doesn''t do any of those things for me.</td>', 'For a candid to work it should provoke some sort of emotional response in the viewer. Generally, there is an element of the unexpected or the subject is captured revealing a strong emotion,i.e., glee, anger, frustration. This just doesn''t do any of those things for me.', '2006-04-12 18:54:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(2307989, 319649, 34192, '<td valign="top">I like this.  Wish the POV was just a little lower, but this works. 7</td>', 'I like this.  Wish the POV was just a little lower, but this works. 7', '2006-04-12 18:54:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(2307990, 319964, 47117, '<td valign="top">I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry in this challenge.<br/> <br/>Children are so easily captured in a candid. This usually puts me off, but in this shot, I like it. I like it because of the added interest in the loving hand under the chin. It tells me the story. The story is not just a boy crying, which one can see a thousand shots of, but its a boy being comforted. I like that. Just the smallest detail like that can make it a good photo verses an every day snapshot. It''s still just a 6 for me though, but that isn''t bad considering I don''t usually like candid shots of children as they are so easy and not out of the comfort zone. But I feel this one, and that is good. I also like the tones and the crop. Good work here.</td>', 'I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry in this challenge. Children are so easily captured in a candid. This usually puts me off, but in this shot, I like it. I like it because of the added interest in the loving hand under the chin. It tells me the story. The story is not just a boy crying, which one can see a thousand shots of, but its a boy being comforted. I like that. Just the smallest detail like that can make it a good photo verses an every day snapshot. It''s still just a 6 for me though, but that isn''t bad considering I don''t usually like candid shots of children as they are so easy and not out of the comfort zone. But I feel this one, and that is good. I also like the tones and the crop. Good work here.', '2006-04-12 18:55:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(2307993, 319382, 47117, '<td valign="top">I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry in this challenge.<br/> <br/>This is unusual, but unfortunately the focus is on the old book more than the older gentlemen. I would really LOVED to have seen his face.  It is filled with shadows and imagining it more than seeing it in a candid is not to my particular liking. I give it a 5 though.</td>', 'I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry in this challenge. This is unusual, but unfortunately the focus is on the old book more than the older gentlemen. I would really LOVED to have seen his face.  It is filled with shadows and imagining it more than seeing it in a candid is not to my particular liking. I give it a 5 though.', '2006-04-12 18:56:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(2307997, 319153, 34192, '<td valign="top">Good toning, good subject, slightly static by its placement/crop.  DOF well done. 7</td>', 'Good toning, good subject, slightly static by its placement/crop.  DOF well done. 7', '2006-04-12 18:57:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(2307998, 318826, 49773, '<td valign="top">Selective desaturation just doesn''t work for me in this case. Nice candid though!</td>', 'Selective desaturation just doesn''t work for me in this case. Nice candid though!', '2006-04-12 18:57:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(2308001, 318266, 47117, '<td valign="top">I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry in this challenge.<br/> <br/>Ok, well, this is a candid, but not the type of candids that I particularly care to see. This is more of an action &amp; sports photo to me, and I would list it as such, if it were mine, long before I would list it as a candid. So in that, I give it a 4.  I do like it, but it just doesn''t have the interest for me some candids give off.</td>', 'I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry in this challenge. Ok, well, this is a candid, but not the type of candids that I particularly care to see. This is more of an action & sports photo to me, and I would list it as such, if it were mine, long before I would list it as a candid. So in that, I give it a 4.  I do like it, but it just doesn''t have the interest for me some candids give off.', '2006-04-12 18:58:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(2308003, 318501, 43772, '<td valign="top">stunning. So Young, So Beautiful! I wish her the best whoever she may be! I hope she has a copy of this image to show her children and her grandchildren who i pray she one day meets! 10</td>', 'stunning. So Young, So Beautiful! I wish her the best whoever she may be! I hope she has a copy of this image to show her children and her grandchildren who i pray she one day meets! 10', '2006-04-12 18:59:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(2308006, 317705, 34192, '<td valign="top">Excellent moment.  Lots of jpeg artifacts but they are subdued by the eyes of the subject (not as noticible).  Well captured. 7</td>', 'Excellent moment.  Lots of jpeg artifacts but they are subdued by the eyes of the subject (not as noticible).  Well captured. 7', '2006-04-12 18:59:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(2308011, 318869, 47117, '<td valign="top">I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry in this challenge.<br/> <br/>Children are so easy to get candids of. Too easy for my liking in a candid I''m afraid, especially from the back. However, with that said, this is good in that it does portray that the little girl is thinking about something. A bit of interest there for me, but it doesn''t scream candid to me in how I particularly care to see them. It''s a 4 photo for me.</td>', 'I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry in this challenge. Children are so easy to get candids of. Too easy for my liking in a candid I''m afraid, especially from the back. However, with that said, this is good in that it does portray that the little girl is thinking about something. A bit of interest there for me, but it doesn''t scream candid to me in how I particularly care to see them. It''s a 4 photo for me.', '2006-04-12 19:00:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(2308012, 316958, 34192, '<td valign="top">Excellent scene.  I can just picture what you could do with this with the advantage of advanced (the dark on the right).  Extremely well composed, color well done, clarity excellent. 9</td>', 'Excellent scene.  I can just picture what you could do with this with the advantage of advanced (the dark on the right).  Extremely well composed, color well done, clarity excellent. 9', '2006-04-12 19:00:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(2308015, 318177, 34192, '<td valign="top">This works for me.  Tones well done, composition good, DOF excellent.  Wish you had gotten a little lower with your POV but this works. 7</td>', 'This works for me.  Tones well done, composition good, DOF excellent.  Wish you had gotten a little lower with your POV but this works. 7', '2006-04-12 19:01:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(2308017, 319365, 34192, '<td valign="top">Good scene.  Wish POV were a little lower but this works.  A little too contrasty for me but it could be my monitor.  Composition and DOF work well. 7</td>', 'Good scene.  Wish POV were a little lower but this works.  A little too contrasty for me but it could be my monitor.  Composition and DOF work well. 7', '2006-04-12 19:02:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(2308018, 318807, 47117, '<td valign="top">I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry in this challenge.<br/> <br/>This is ok. Good dof. Tons of shadows on the faces, but we can''t always control where the sun will shine when taking a candid.  Of course, sunglasses are always a nightmare to candid photographers as well.  I also see little emotion here. Other than the hug I see little interest. I can however, imagine them seeing something or watching something emotional.  It is just a bit of a stretch for me though to imagine when I like to see it head on.  It''s a 5 photo for me.</td>', 'I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry in this challenge. This is ok. Good dof. Tons of shadows on the faces, but we can''t always control where the sun will shine when taking a candid.  Of course, sunglasses are always a nightmare to candid photographers as well.  I also see little emotion here. Other than the hug I see little interest. I can however, imagine them seeing something or watching something emotional.  It is just a bit of a stretch for me though to imagine when I like to see it head on.  It''s a 5 photo for me.', '2006-04-12 19:02:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(2308022, 319949, 34192, '<td valign="top">Too soft, too close, blah, blah blah...  I like this.  The softness works with the moment and is very effective for this image.  Composition extremely well done, toning excellent. 8</td>', 'Too soft, too close, blah, blah blah...  I like this.  The softness works with the moment and is very effective for this image.  Composition extremely well done, toning excellent. 8', '2006-04-12 19:03:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(2308028, 320014, 34192, '<td valign="top">The lighting makes the image.  And it is excellent here.  Great expression, muted colors work well.  Composition excellent 8</td>', 'The lighting makes the image.  And it is excellent here.  Great expression, muted colors work well.  Composition excellent 8', '2006-04-12 19:05:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(2308029, 319682, 47117, '<td valign="top">I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry in this challenge.<br/> <br/>Children are so easy to capture in a candid. They rarely hold back emotion and always tend to be doing something out of the ordinary from adults.  In that, candids with children, to me, must have something exceptional going on in order for me to feel interest from them. This is ok. It does show emotion in the eyes, but it isn''t exceptional to me or anything out of the ordinary.  It''s just an ok candid. It''s a 4 from me.</td>', 'I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry in this challenge. Children are so easy to capture in a candid. They rarely hold back emotion and always tend to be doing something out of the ordinary from adults.  In that, candids with children, to me, must have something exceptional going on in order for me to feel interest from them. This is ok. It does show emotion in the eyes, but it isn''t exceptional to me or anything out of the ordinary.  It''s just an ok candid. It''s a 4 from me.', '2006-04-12 19:05:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(2308035, 319618, 47117, '<td valign="top">I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry in this challenge.<br/> <br/>This is a good candid, but lacks focus on the subject technically.  But I like the interest. I gave it a 4.</td>', 'I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry in this challenge. This is a good candid, but lacks focus on the subject technically.  But I like the interest. I gave it a 4.', '2006-04-12 19:06:15.000000', NULL, 1),
