(2310109, 319035, 47117, '<td valign="top">I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are <br/>near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry <br/>in this challenge.<br/> <br/>This is just ok for me. A photograph of another photographer really is pretty uninteresting to me unless that photographer is doing something extra ordinary. In this shot he is just looking at something, but he is out of focus.  His face does exude some emotion, but not enough to really grasp what I find appealing in a candid.  I like to see things that are obscure, out of the ordinary and every-day realm, and/or that give me a sense of a one-time capture.  This is a 3 for me I''m afraid.</td>', 'I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry in this challenge. This is just ok for me. A photograph of another photographer really is pretty uninteresting to me unless that photographer is doing something extra ordinary. In this shot he is just looking at something, but he is out of focus.  His face does exude some emotion, but not enough to really grasp what I find appealing in a candid.  I like to see things that are obscure, out of the ordinary and every-day realm, and/or that give me a sense of a one-time capture.  This is a 3 for me I''m afraid.', '2006-04-13 13:43:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(2310113, 318869, 48339, '<td valign="top">everything is great about this shot, but it''s sooo grainy and pixally it really takes away from the quality. if the shot were crisp and clean it would do very well.</td>', 'everything is great about this shot, but it''s sooo grainy and pixally it really takes away from the quality. if the shot were crisp and clean it would do very well.', '2006-04-13 13:46:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(2310115, 320017, 47117, '<td valign="top">I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are <br/>near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry <br/>in this challenge.<br/> <br/>Children are prime targets for candids. They are sweet and innocent and are really a dream for anyone who likes children candids or likes to learn first with children on how to get a candid before tackling the harder job at hand, which is candids of adults.  I personally prefer to see shots that are more out of that comfort zone. Children don''t usually shy away from the camera, nor usually from the world, and will do many things in public you wouldn''t necessarily find any adult doing.  For me, this shot is typical of any children candid. For me it''s a 3 vote I''m afraid. Cute, but not all that interesting enough for my liking.</td>', 'I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry in this challenge. Children are prime targets for candids. They are sweet and innocent and are really a dream for anyone who likes children candids or likes to learn first with children on how to get a candid before tackling the harder job at hand, which is candids of adults.  I personally prefer to see shots that are more out of that comfort zone. Children don''t usually shy away from the camera, nor usually from the world, and will do many things in public you wouldn''t necessarily find any adult doing.  For me, this shot is typical of any children candid. For me it''s a 3 vote I''m afraid. Cute, but not all that interesting enough for my liking.', '2006-04-13 13:46:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(2310117, 318354, 53147, '<td valign="top">Great capture. You would almost think that this had to be a posed shot considering the vast difference in facial expressions between the two. I really liked the comparison of the two sides - happy and bright to darker and more gloomy.</td>', 'Great capture. You would almost think that this had to be a posed shot considering the vast difference in facial expressions between the two. I really liked the comparison of the two sides - happy and bright to darker and more gloomy.', '2006-04-13 13:47:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(2310124, 318143, 48339, '<td valign="top">a mecca of candids is all around this shot, but not in it. kinda just feels like a ''head cam'' shot without the life of the city.  average. 5</td>', 'a mecca of candids is all around this shot, but not in it. kinda just feels like a ''head cam'' shot without the life of the city.  average. 5', '2006-04-13 13:49:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(2310125, 318058, 56735, '<td valign="top">Today, even a beginner can take professional quality pictures, with correct exposures, meterings, etc. However, this is not totally true.<br/> <br/>Anybody can buy a sophisticated camera and take pro-quality pics, but the difference between two photographers, or more perticularly, two images, of the same shot lies in the eyes of the photographers. Composition is the key to ones success these days, as Adobe Photoshop and other softwares cannot compose the images also!<br/> <br/>Bravo to the great photographer. Even a few pics of Cecil Beaton has failed to satisfy me recently, but this pic, indeed managed to satisfy me. Ahh...what freshness! My best wishes for you.</td>', 'Today, even a beginner can take professional quality pictures, with correct exposures, meterings, etc. However, this is not totally true. Anybody can buy a sophisticated camera and take pro-quality pics, but the difference between two photographers, or more perticularly, two images, of the same shot lies in the eyes of the photographers. Composition is the key to ones success these days, as Adobe Photoshop and other softwares cannot compose the images also! Bravo to the great photographer. Even a few pics of Cecil Beaton has failed to satisfy me recently, but this pic, indeed managed to satisfy me. Ahh...what freshness! My best wishes for you.', '2006-04-13 13:49:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(2310128, 319494, 48339, '<td valign="top">convincing glare.</td>', 'convincing glare.', '2006-04-13 13:51:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(2310130, 318749, 47117, '<td valign="top">I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are <br/>near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry <br/>in this challenge.<br/> <br/>Ok, well, children are far too easy to get candids of. They do all kinds of obscure and out of the ordinary things in and out of public on any given day.  Here we have a child, but not one doing anything extra ordinary, but just walking down the street. I would have totally cropped this to the top of his head leaving only the street in the shot with him top left of the frame. I would have converted it to b/w and given a lot of attention to Highlight, Shadow, and Midtones to really bring out the texture of the road and his clothing and hair.  I would have also given it a good dash of unsharp mask, as it is out of focus. To me that would have made this shot a bit more interesting. It would have made the viewer wonder where he was going. In this shot, nothing is left to mystery. There is no interest here at all for me other than a shot of a child walking. As is, and as a candid, this is a 3 for me.</td>', 'I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry in this challenge. Ok, well, children are far too easy to get candids of. They do all kinds of obscure and out of the ordinary things in and out of public on any given day.  Here we have a child, but not one doing anything extra ordinary, but just walking down the street. I would have totally cropped this to the top of his head leaving only the street in the shot with him top left of the frame. I would have converted it to b/w and given a lot of attention to Highlight, Shadow, and Midtones to really bring out the texture of the road and his clothing and hair.  I would have also given it a good dash of unsharp mask, as it is out of focus. To me that would have made this shot a bit more interesting. It would have made the viewer wonder where he was going. In this shot, nothing is left to mystery. There is no interest here at all for me other than a shot of a child walking. As is, and as a candid, this is a 3 for me.', '2006-04-13 13:51:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(2310133, 320040, 48339, '<td valign="top">cute.</td>', 'cute.', '2006-04-13 13:52:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(2310135, 318977, 47117, '<td valign="top">I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are <br/>near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry <br/>in this challenge.<br/> <br/>Children are far to easy to get candids of for my liking. The zoo, or at any event, they are even more easily captured.  I really see nothing here that interests me personally in what I expect from a candid. I like to see people out of the ordinary, something obscure, something to make the mind stimulated by the view.  This to me is any typical snapshot one can take at any zoo with any child at any time of the day. It''s a 3 for me.</td>', 'I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry in this challenge. Children are far to easy to get candids of for my liking. The zoo, or at any event, they are even more easily captured.  I really see nothing here that interests me personally in what I expect from a candid. I like to see people out of the ordinary, something obscure, something to make the mind stimulated by the view.  This to me is any typical snapshot one can take at any zoo with any child at any time of the day. It''s a 3 for me.', '2006-04-13 13:53:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(2310137, 319913, 47117, '<td valign="top">I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are <br/>near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry <br/>in this challenge.<br/> <br/>Well, I like the tones, but the shot is out of focus and really holds no interest for me in what I like and expect from a candid. It''s just a guy with his dog. I like to see things more unexpected, people out of the ordinary, obscure situations, something that stimulates more interest. I get no real wow factors from this. It is a 3 for me.</td>', 'I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry in this challenge. Well, I like the tones, but the shot is out of focus and really holds no interest for me in what I like and expect from a candid. It''s just a guy with his dog. I like to see things more unexpected, people out of the ordinary, obscure situations, something that stimulates more interest. I get no real wow factors from this. It is a 3 for me.', '2006-04-13 13:55:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(2310138, 318388, 48339, '<td valign="top">excellent capture.. maybe just a little closer would be a real wow..7</td>', 'excellent capture.. maybe just a little closer would be a real wow..7', '2006-04-13 13:56:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(2310139, 319579, 47117, '<td valign="top">I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are <br/>near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry <br/>in this challenge.<br/> <br/>This is just ok for me.  But it holds little interest for me as a candid. It is two people sitting on a park bench, and neither have any real expression going on. I like to see in a candid something more obscure, out of the ordinary, something that causes my eye to be stimulated. This just doesn''t do it for me. It''s a 3 vote.</td>', 'I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry in this challenge. This is just ok for me.  But it holds little interest for me as a candid. It is two people sitting on a park bench, and neither have any real expression going on. I like to see in a candid something more obscure, out of the ordinary, something that causes my eye to be stimulated. This just doesn''t do it for me. It''s a 3 vote.', '2006-04-13 13:56:29.000000', NULL, 1),
