(2310159, 320015, 7322, '<td valign="top">The umbrellas and the blurry bits in the lower corners create confusion and clutter which ruins this for me.</td>', 'The umbrellas and the blurry bits in the lower corners create confusion and clutter which ruins this for me.', '2006-04-13 14:08:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(2310162, 320051, 48339, '<td valign="top">i can sniff a set-up shot. and it''s not that good anyway.</td>', 'i can sniff a set-up shot. and it''s not that good anyway.', '2006-04-13 14:09:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(2310167, 319936, 7322, '<td valign="top">This is very for me. I think the vertical format was a poor choice for this scene as it cramps everything in. It would have been more interesting to see the girl reacting to the playing field below than seeing the  people in the stands over her head. If the field were included the viewers eye would have a more natural progression to follow--from the girl, to what the girl is responding to. Instead, the viewers eye is led upward to the other attendees who don''t provide any interest or answers.</td>', 'This is very for me. I think the vertical format was a poor choice for this scene as it cramps everything in. It would have been more interesting to see the girl reacting to the playing field below than seeing the  people in the stands over her head. If the field were included the viewers eye would have a more natural progression to follow--from the girl, to what the girl is responding to. Instead, the viewers eye is led upward to the other attendees who don''t provide any interest or answers.', '2006-04-13 14:14:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(2310168, 319923, 47117, '<td valign="top">I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are <br/>near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry <br/>in this challenge.<br/> <br/>Children are far too easy to get candids of in my opinion. They can be found doing all kinds of obscure things on a daily basis with little regard to what is around them or who.  Their emotions, unlike adults, are not contained.  With that said, I do like your photo, but it just doesn''t have that kick for me I personally prefer to see in a candid.  I prefer to see something out of the ordinary, something obscure, something that sparks more of an interest in seeing a none every day thing going on.  The unexpected.  The child is cute, and you did very well in using the b/w tones.  But as a candid its a 3 vote for me.</td>', 'I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry in this challenge. Children are far too easy to get candids of in my opinion. They can be found doing all kinds of obscure things on a daily basis with little regard to what is around them or who.  Their emotions, unlike adults, are not contained.  With that said, I do like your photo, but it just doesn''t have that kick for me I personally prefer to see in a candid.  I prefer to see something out of the ordinary, something obscure, something that sparks more of an interest in seeing a none every day thing going on.  The unexpected.  The child is cute, and you did very well in using the b/w tones.  But as a candid its a 3 vote for me.', '2006-04-13 14:15:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(2310175, 319684, 7322, '<td valign="top">The background is too cluttered for me and while the girl has a pleasant smile, she is looking off camera and she was captured in an awkward stance that doesn''t really reveal much about her enjoyment or the exhuberence of sliding. I think placing yourself at the bottom and timing the shot so you could catch the girl''s expression in mid slide would have created a far more dynamic and interesting photo for the objective viewer.</td>', 'The background is too cluttered for me and while the girl has a pleasant smile, she is looking off camera and she was captured in an awkward stance that doesn''t really reveal much about her enjoyment or the exhuberence of sliding. I think placing yourself at the bottom and timing the shot so you could catch the girl''s expression in mid slide would have created a far more dynamic and interesting photo for the objective viewer.', '2006-04-13 14:19:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(2310176, 317907, 47117, '<td valign="top">I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are <br/>near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry <br/>in this challenge.<br/> <br/>This is ok for me. Since children are so easy to get candids of, I am a little surprised to see this so out of focus, but it is nice. Just a bit too easy for my liking.  I like to see more of people doing extra ordinary things, more interest, something that sparks the mind a bit more. To me this is just a bit too ordinary.  It''s a 3 for me.</td>', 'I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry in this challenge. This is ok for me. Since children are so easy to get candids of, I am a little surprised to see this so out of focus, but it is nice. Just a bit too easy for my liking.  I like to see more of people doing extra ordinary things, more interest, something that sparks the mind a bit more. To me this is just a bit too ordinary.  It''s a 3 for me.', '2006-04-13 14:20:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(2310185, 318809, 7322, '<td valign="top">It would have been more interesting to me if you included a view of some of the skaters in action. It is generally not a great idea to show everyone in a group of people looking off-camera unless you involve the viewer by showing what everyone is looking at, or unless one of the subjects is looking at the camera in some way which draws the viewer in, or looking off in an unexpected direction that adds something humorous to the shot. This sort of shot tends to be very impersonal to the objective viewer.</td>', 'It would have been more interesting to me if you included a view of some of the skaters in action. It is generally not a great idea to show everyone in a group of people looking off-camera unless you involve the viewer by showing what everyone is looking at, or unless one of the subjects is looking at the camera in some way which draws the viewer in, or looking off in an unexpected direction that adds something humorous to the shot. This sort of shot tends to be very impersonal to the objective viewer.', '2006-04-13 14:25:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(2310186, 320048, 13759, '<td valign="top">I´m curious about your lenses! What interesting boke it is.</td>', 'I´m curious about your lenses! What interesting boke it is.', '2006-04-13 14:25:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(2310191, 319980, 47117, '<td valign="top">I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are <br/>near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry <br/>in this challenge.<br/> <br/>For me the only thing that really makes this photo is the tones. Good lighting and good tones. I''m afraid that other than that, to me it is just some people sitting somewhere for lunch or coffee. Nothing really obscure, nothing really of interest for me here I''m afraid. It''s just ok, but it really has no kick for me.  It''s a 3 photo for me in this challenge.</td>', 'I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry in this challenge. For me the only thing that really makes this photo is the tones. Good lighting and good tones. I''m afraid that other than that, to me it is just some people sitting somewhere for lunch or coffee. Nothing really obscure, nothing really of interest for me here I''m afraid. It''s just ok, but it really has no kick for me.  It''s a 3 photo for me in this challenge.', '2006-04-13 14:27:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(2310193, 318306, 47117, '<td valign="top">I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are <br/>near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry <br/>in this challenge.<br/> <br/>Children are far too easy to capture in a candid. They are willing to not hold back emotion or do obscure things. They are fun to learn about candid shooting, but for me, I look for something more obscure, extra ordinary, and/or that sparks a stimulating interest in a candid. For me this is also out of focus and not very well done technically. More attention to sharpness would have been a bit better. I think the branches may have caused that, as it tends to cause the focus to wonder in the camera. It''a a 3 for me.</td>', 'I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry in this challenge. Children are far too easy to capture in a candid. They are willing to not hold back emotion or do obscure things. They are fun to learn about candid shooting, but for me, I look for something more obscure, extra ordinary, and/or that sparks a stimulating interest in a candid. For me this is also out of focus and not very well done technically. More attention to sharpness would have been a bit better. I think the branches may have caused that, as it tends to cause the focus to wonder in the camera. It''a a 3 for me.', '2006-04-13 14:30:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(2310196, 319587, 47117, '<td valign="top">I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are <br/>near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry <br/>in this challenge.<br/> <br/>This is just alright for me. It has decent focus, color and lighting. However, when I look at it as a candid, I really don''t feel the need to say "wow, that is good" or cool or a great shot of a candid. I like to see more interest, something a bit more obscure, and/or something out of the ordinary.  So for me this is a 4 vote.</td>', 'I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry in this challenge. This is just alright for me. It has decent focus, color and lighting. However, when I look at it as a candid, I really don''t feel the need to say "wow, that is good" or cool or a great shot of a candid. I like to see more interest, something a bit more obscure, and/or something out of the ordinary.  So for me this is a 4 vote.', '2006-04-13 14:31:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(2310200, 318000, 47117, '<td valign="top">I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are <br/>near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry <br/>in this challenge.<br/> <br/>Well, this challenge was really about capturing a candid, and not about power and beauty and how they equate to each other.  Glasses and hats are a nightmare to the candid photographer. They mask emotion in many cases, and this photo is a prime example.  I see little emotion or anything that shouts at me. Little interest, nothing extra ordinary, nothing out of the every day realm, or anything that even gives me a feeling for what she is thinking or any story.  To me this is a 3 for a candid challenge. I would like to also have seen more focus in play for this shot.</td>', 'I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry in this challenge. Well, this challenge was really about capturing a candid, and not about power and beauty and how they equate to each other.  Glasses and hats are a nightmare to the candid photographer. They mask emotion in many cases, and this photo is a prime example.  I see little emotion or anything that shouts at me. Little interest, nothing extra ordinary, nothing out of the every day realm, or anything that even gives me a feeling for what she is thinking or any story.  To me this is a 3 for a candid challenge. I would like to also have seen more focus in play for this shot.', '2006-04-13 14:34:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(2310202, 319977, 47117, '<td valign="top">I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are <br/>near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry <br/>in this challenge.<br/> <br/>This is just ok for me. Not really much interest.  It''s a bit bland. No story, nothing out of the ordinary, no emotions, and just someone reading. Lots of dead space is ok for this shot, but as a candid I really don''t like much but the tones. I need something a bit more of interest in what I like to see in a candid. I gave it a 3.</td>', 'I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry in this challenge. This is just ok for me. Not really much interest.  It''s a bit bland. No story, nothing out of the ordinary, no emotions, and just someone reading. Lots of dead space is ok for this shot, but as a candid I really don''t like much but the tones. I need something a bit more of interest in what I like to see in a candid. I gave it a 3.', '2006-04-13 14:36:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(2310203, 319601, 7322, '<td valign="top">This looks like a snapshot and not a particularly good one, I''m sorry to say. The background is too cluttered and the image is overly contrasty, i.e., blown out in the highlight areas and too dark in the shadow areas. If you had not included the title I would have thought this was a snap that caught the subject in mid-blink --- it''s not a very flattering photo of the little girl. Next time, try to be aware of what you are including in the frame when you compose a shot. It is easy for the mind''s eye to ignore a distracting background but the camera sees it all. As far as the contrasty image goes, it is a contrasty scene and difficult to shoot using automatic exposure settings. Your camera should have a basic EV mode which allows you to bracket exposures in this type of difficult lighting situation. It also helps to use some sort of reflector near the subject. This can be as simple as a sheet of white poster board, as is, or wrapped with aluminum foil.</td>', 'This looks like a snapshot and not a particularly good one, I''m sorry to say. The background is too cluttered and the image is overly contrasty, i.e., blown out in the highlight areas and too dark in the shadow areas. If you had not included the title I would have thought this was a snap that caught the subject in mid-blink --- it''s not a very flattering photo of the little girl. Next time, try to be aware of what you are including in the frame when you compose a shot. It is easy for the mind''s eye to ignore a distracting background but the camera sees it all. As far as the contrasty image goes, it is a contrasty scene and difficult to shoot using automatic exposure settings. Your camera should have a basic EV mode which allows you to bracket exposures in this type of difficult lighting situation. It also helps to use some sort of reflector near the subject. This can be as simple as a sheet of white poster board, as is, or wrapped with aluminum foil.', '2006-04-13 14:37:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(2310205, 319937, 47117, '<td valign="top">I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are <br/>near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry <br/>in this challenge.<br/> <br/>This is really not to my liking for a candid. It''s a bit dark for starters, but then I see absolutely no story, no real emotion, nothing out of the ordinary, nothing obscure.  Just holds little interest for me. It''a 3 vote.</td>', 'I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry in this challenge. This is really not to my liking for a candid. It''s a bit dark for starters, but then I see absolutely no story, no real emotion, nothing out of the ordinary, nothing obscure.  Just holds little interest for me. It''a 3 vote.', '2006-04-13 14:37:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(2310207, 320040, 7322, '<td valign="top">Fun, quirky angle and great capture of her expression. Her crazy hat adds interest and a bit of framing, as well as blocking out a potentially distracting background. I''ll forgive the hokey title.</td>', 'Fun, quirky angle and great capture of her expression. Her crazy hat adds interest and a bit of framing, as well as blocking out a potentially distracting background. I''ll forgive the hokey title.', '2006-04-13 14:38:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(2310210, 319482, 47117, '<td valign="top">I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are <br/>near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry <br/>in this challenge.<br/> <br/>This is ok, but badly composed I''m afraid. The skin tones are far too red, and the greens aren''t nearly green enough, and more could have been done with tones and color here.  I probably would have converted it to b/w or sepia with attention to H/M/S. Glasses are a nightmare for the candid photographer also. They mask emotion in most cases, unless you can see the expression through them or other things are going on around them. I see nothing that sparks any real interest in this shot for me, and what is there is really ruined for me in technicals.  I''m afraid this is a 3 vote for me.</td>', 'I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry in this challenge. This is ok, but badly composed I''m afraid. The skin tones are far too red, and the greens aren''t nearly green enough, and more could have been done with tones and color here.  I probably would have converted it to b/w or sepia with attention to H/M/S. Glasses are a nightmare for the candid photographer also. They mask emotion in most cases, unless you can see the expression through them or other things are going on around them. I see nothing that sparks any real interest in this shot for me, and what is there is really ruined for me in technicals.  I''m afraid this is a 3 vote for me.', '2006-04-13 14:40:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(2310211, 320040, 47117, '<td valign="top">I don''t usually like comments or give them, but since candids are near and dear to my heart, I have decided to comment on every photo in this challenge.<br/> <br/>This is ok, but children and candids go hand in hand really. No big wow factors for me. I could have gotten a million of them this week with my own son, but I prefer with an actual candid challenge to step out of the comfort zone. I gave this photo a 3. It''s cute, but just ok.</td>', 'I don''t usually like comments or give them, but since candids are near and dear to my heart, I have decided to comment on every photo in this challenge. This is ok, but children and candids go hand in hand really. No big wow factors for me. I could have gotten a million of them this week with my own son, but I prefer with an actual candid challenge to step out of the comfort zone. I gave this photo a 3. It''s cute, but just ok.', '2006-04-13 14:40:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(2310212, 319550, 7322, '<td valign="top">I like the inclusion of the horse as it adds a sense of place. Her expressioon is great but I''d like to see who or what she is responding to and pleased about. I''d sacrifice the horse to be included more.</td>', 'I like the inclusion of the horse as it adds a sense of place. Her expressioon is great but I''d like to see who or what she is responding to and pleased about. I''d sacrifice the horse to be included more.', '2006-04-13 14:40:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(2310216, 319731, 47117, '<td valign="top">I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are <br/>near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry <br/>in this challenge.<br/> <br/>Children in candids are prime targets. This one, I''m afraid, is not well composed. No facial expression, little to no story, dark, little interest.  What I like to see in candids is not snapshots of children or family or friends or even strangers. I like to see something out of the ordinary, the unexpected, something that tells a story or sparks stimulation to the eye.  Here, to me, this is just a snapshot that was badly composed. It''s a 3 for me.</td>', 'I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry in this challenge. Children in candids are prime targets. This one, I''m afraid, is not well composed. No facial expression, little to no story, dark, little interest.  What I like to see in candids is not snapshots of children or family or friends or even strangers. I like to see something out of the ordinary, the unexpected, something that tells a story or sparks stimulation to the eye.  Here, to me, this is just a snapshot that was badly composed. It''s a 3 for me.', '2006-04-13 14:43:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(2310217, 319219, 47117, '<td valign="top">I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are <br/>near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry <br/>in this challenge.<br/> <br/>To me, fancy dress and makeup don''t always make a good candid. It is nice and shows some interest, but I like to see a bit more. Something out of the ordinary, something more obscure, and/or something unexpected going on then a speaker or a performer.  To me this is some kind of performance. It is a candid, but just not what I care to see in one. For me it is a 3 vote.</td>', 'I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry in this challenge. To me, fancy dress and makeup don''t always make a good candid. It is nice and shows some interest, but I like to see a bit more. Something out of the ordinary, something more obscure, and/or something unexpected going on then a speaker or a performer.  To me this is some kind of performance. It is a candid, but just not what I care to see in one. For me it is a 3 vote.', '2006-04-13 14:45:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(2310219, 319316, 47117, '<td valign="top">I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are <br/>near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry <br/>in this challenge.<br/> <br/>To me, this is more portrait then candid, although it is a candid look. Children are far too easy to get candids from, and this is really no exception. I really don''t find much interest in this shot as a candid. She is darling, but what I care to see in a candid is something a bit more out of the ordinary, that sparks an interest or emotion that one wouldn''t normally see every day or notice every day, and/or something with a bit of a story or kick to it.  This is a 3 for me.</td>', 'I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry in this challenge. To me, this is more portrait then candid, although it is a candid look. Children are far too easy to get candids from, and this is really no exception. I really don''t find much interest in this shot as a candid. She is darling, but what I care to see in a candid is something a bit more out of the ordinary, that sparks an interest or emotion that one wouldn''t normally see every day or notice every day, and/or something with a bit of a story or kick to it.  This is a 3 for me.', '2006-04-13 14:47:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(2310222, 319365, 47117, '<td valign="top">I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are <br/>near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry <br/>in this challenge.<br/> <br/>This is ok. Perhaps more focus on the man was in order. It seems the cameras focus wandered to the seating before him. I do like the tones, but I can''t really grasp any real interest for me here. It''s a 4 from me.</td>', 'I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry in this challenge. This is ok. Perhaps more focus on the man was in order. It seems the cameras focus wandered to the seating before him. I do like the tones, but I can''t really grasp any real interest for me here. It''s a 4 from me.', '2006-04-13 14:49:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(2310224, 319915, 47117, '<td valign="top">I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are <br/>near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry <br/>in this challenge.<br/> <br/>Children are far to easy to get candids of in my opinion. They are prime targets and do lots of precious things every day. This is no exception. However, in a candid, I like to see something more out of the ordinary, or obscure, or something that tells a story and/or sparks stimulation or emotion.  To me this is just not what I look for in a candid. It''s a 3 for me.</td>', 'I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry in this challenge. Children are far to easy to get candids of in my opinion. They are prime targets and do lots of precious things every day. This is no exception. However, in a candid, I like to see something more out of the ordinary, or obscure, or something that tells a story and/or sparks stimulation or emotion.  To me this is just not what I look for in a candid. It''s a 3 for me.', '2006-04-13 14:51:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(2310228, 319601, 47117, '<td valign="top">I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are <br/>near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry <br/>in this challenge.<br/> <br/>Besides the fact that children are far too easy to get candids of, this shot is too small and had unfortunate technical problems. The lighting is too harsh in some areas where as the shadows are too over powering in other areas.  As a candid, it holds little to no interest for me. I look for something out of the ordinary, obscure, that sparks emotion in me by the subject or composition, and this just doesn''t do it I''m afraid. It''s a 3 from me.</td>', 'I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry in this challenge. Besides the fact that children are far too easy to get candids of, this shot is too small and had unfortunate technical problems. The lighting is too harsh in some areas where as the shadows are too over powering in other areas.  As a candid, it holds little to no interest for me. I look for something out of the ordinary, obscure, that sparks emotion in me by the subject or composition, and this just doesn''t do it I''m afraid. It''s a 3 from me.', '2006-04-13 14:53:25.000000', NULL, 1),
