(2322179, 319233, 47117, '<td valign="top">I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are <br/>near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry <br/>in this challenge.<br/> <br/>Nice dof on the flower, but I don''t really see this as a candid. Children and candids really go hand in hand, as they do not really contain their emotions or actions. This does tell a bit of a story, but I do believe the child is awares of the camera. I prefer to see a bit more a comfort zone lost for the photograher.</td>', 'I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry in this challenge. Nice dof on the flower, but I don''t really see this as a candid. Children and candids really go hand in hand, as they do not really contain their emotions or actions. This does tell a bit of a story, but I do believe the child is awares of the camera. I prefer to see a bit more a comfort zone lost for the photograher.', '2006-04-18 15:34:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(2322180, 319930, 47117, '<td valign="top">I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are <br/>near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry <br/>in this challenge.<br/> <br/>Unfortunately this is one of those photos that looks great as a thumbnail, but has great problems at full size. It is entirely out of focus and over exposed.  Also, as a candid, I see very little of interest. A couple from the back holding hands is really not a very good candid shot I''m afraid, in how I recognize one photographically. No real interest, no real story, nothing out of the ordinary going on.  This is a 2 for me.</td>', 'I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry in this challenge. Unfortunately this is one of those photos that looks great as a thumbnail, but has great problems at full size. It is entirely out of focus and over exposed.  Also, as a candid, I see very little of interest. A couple from the back holding hands is really not a very good candid shot I''m afraid, in how I recognize one photographically. No real interest, no real story, nothing out of the ordinary going on.  This is a 2 for me.', '2006-04-18 15:34:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(2322181, 319955, 47117, '<td valign="top">I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are <br/>near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry <br/>in this challenge.<br/> <br/>Unfortunately, candids of animals are really not what I look for in a good candid. Animals are aware and both unaware at the same time of a photographer, nor do they care either way.  Too easy, no comfort zone lost. It''s a 2 for me.</td>', 'I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry in this challenge. Unfortunately, candids of animals are really not what I look for in a good candid. Animals are aware and both unaware at the same time of a photographer, nor do they care either way.  Too easy, no comfort zone lost. It''s a 2 for me.', '2006-04-18 15:34:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(2322182, 318593, 47117, '<td valign="top">I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are <br/>near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry <br/>in this challenge.<br/> <br/>A beautiful child and photo, but its a portrait to me and not a candid.  A candid, to me, has something within that is out of the ordinary, draws interest by situation, or interest by subject matter. To me this is a child who is lovely but contains not any of which I mention.  It''s a 2 for me.</td>', 'I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry in this challenge. A beautiful child and photo, but its a portrait to me and not a candid.  A candid, to me, has something within that is out of the ordinary, draws interest by situation, or interest by subject matter. To me this is a child who is lovely but contains not any of which I mention.  It''s a 2 for me.', '2006-04-18 15:34:25.000000', NULL, 1);
INSERT INTO comments ("id", "image_id", "commenter_id", "raw_comment", "comment", "date", "edited", "made_during_challenge") VALUES
(2322183, 320015, 47117, '<td valign="top">I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are <br/>near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry <br/>in this challenge.<br/> <br/>Unfortunately, candids of animals are really not what I look for in a good candid. Animals are aware and both unaware at the same time of a photographer, nor do they care either way.  Too easy, no comfort zone lost. It''s a 2 for me.</td>', 'I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry in this challenge. Unfortunately, candids of animals are really not what I look for in a good candid. Animals are aware and both unaware at the same time of a photographer, nor do they care either way.  Too easy, no comfort zone lost. It''s a 2 for me.', '2006-04-18 15:34:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(2322189, 319388, 47117, '<td valign="top">I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are <br/>near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry <br/>in this challenge.<br/> <br/>This is just ok as a candid for me. I prefer, myself, not to see candids of children unless they are doing something out of the ordinary and to the extreme. Children tend to not contain emotions or actions, so they are prime targets for candids. I prefer a bit of a comfort zone lost to the candid photographer. Technically, this photo is not well done. No really focus and the lighting is pretty off. Cute boy though!</td>', 'I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry in this challenge. This is just ok as a candid for me. I prefer, myself, not to see candids of children unless they are doing something out of the ordinary and to the extreme. Children tend to not contain emotions or actions, so they are prime targets for candids. I prefer a bit of a comfort zone lost to the candid photographer. Technically, this photo is not well done. No really focus and the lighting is pretty off. Cute boy though!', '2006-04-18 15:36:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(2322190, 318918, 47117, '<td valign="top">I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are <br/>near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry <br/>in this challenge.<br/> <br/>A cute child, however, it is a bit out of focus and basically a snapshot. Children are far too easy to capture candids of. They virtually have their emotions and actions uncontained, verses that of adults.  For me, I prefer to see something out of the ordinary, that tells more of a story, or has great interest in subject matter or situation for a candid.  If I were to list this shot in a category, it would be under family and not candid. This a 2 for me.</td>', 'I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry in this challenge. A cute child, however, it is a bit out of focus and basically a snapshot. Children are far too easy to capture candids of. They virtually have their emotions and actions uncontained, verses that of adults.  For me, I prefer to see something out of the ordinary, that tells more of a story, or has great interest in subject matter or situation for a candid.  If I were to list this shot in a category, it would be under family and not candid. This a 2 for me.', '2006-04-18 15:36:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(2322191, 319214, 47117, '<td valign="top">I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are <br/>near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry <br/>in this challenge.<br/> <br/>Not a very good candid here I''m afraid. The woman is too far back and obscured.  The hand over the eyes masks any emotion. No real story, kick, or interest to the shot. It''s a nice building with character, but as a candid, it does very little for me. It''s a 2.</td>', 'I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry in this challenge. Not a very good candid here I''m afraid. The woman is too far back and obscured.  The hand over the eyes masks any emotion. No real story, kick, or interest to the shot. It''s a nice building with character, but as a candid, it does very little for me. It''s a 2.', '2006-04-18 15:36:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(2322194, 319688, 47117, '<td valign="top">I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are <br/>near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry <br/>in this challenge.<br/> <br/>I am not quite sure what is being portrayed here, but as a candid in photography, and how I see it personally, a candid is a moment captured of a person unawares. One that has a bit of a story to it, or an amusing situation, or is out of the ordinary. Candid eyes is not my idea of a good candid shot in that regard.  Pretty eyes, and good focus, but to me not a candid. It''s a 2 for me.</td>', 'I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry in this challenge. I am not quite sure what is being portrayed here, but as a candid in photography, and how I see it personally, a candid is a moment captured of a person unawares. One that has a bit of a story to it, or an amusing situation, or is out of the ordinary. Candid eyes is not my idea of a good candid shot in that regard.  Pretty eyes, and good focus, but to me not a candid. It''s a 2 for me.', '2006-04-18 15:36:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(2322199, 318913, 47117, '<td valign="top">I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are <br/>near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry <br/>in this challenge.<br/> <br/>This is just an ok candid for me. If I were to list it in a category myself, I would list it under b/w and then emotive, but not a candid.  Although it is a candid moment, it is just a bit too expected considering the story the photo tells of the event the child is at.  As for technicals, the focus on the child is good; it has nice tones and good lighting.</td>', 'I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry in this challenge. This is just an ok candid for me. If I were to list it in a category myself, I would list it under b/w and then emotive, but not a candid.  Although it is a candid moment, it is just a bit too expected considering the story the photo tells of the event the child is at.  As for technicals, the focus on the child is good; it has nice tones and good lighting.', '2006-04-18 15:38:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(2322201, 320004, 47117, '<td valign="top">I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are <br/>near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry <br/>in this challenge.<br/> <br/>This is ok, but expected for me. At such events, these types of snapshots are expected. Not something out of the ordinary, or a story told that one hasn''t really seen or heard before from the shot.  I prefer something a bit more out of the ordinary in a candid. Technically, there is little in focus here and the photo is rather small. It''s a 2 for me.</td>', 'I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry in this challenge. This is ok, but expected for me. At such events, these types of snapshots are expected. Not something out of the ordinary, or a story told that one hasn''t really seen or heard before from the shot.  I prefer something a bit more out of the ordinary in a candid. Technically, there is little in focus here and the photo is rather small. It''s a 2 for me.', '2006-04-18 15:38:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(2322205, 319954, 47117, '<td valign="top">I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are <br/>near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry <br/>in this challenge.<br/> <br/>Unfortunately, candids of animals are really not what I look for in a good candid. Animals are aware and both unaware at the same time of a photographer, nor do they care either way.  Too easy, no comfort zone lost. It''s a 2 for me. Cute pet portrait though!</td>', 'I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry in this challenge. Unfortunately, candids of animals are really not what I look for in a good candid. Animals are aware and both unaware at the same time of a photographer, nor do they care either way.  Too easy, no comfort zone lost. It''s a 2 for me. Cute pet portrait though!', '2006-04-18 15:39:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(2322209, 319658, 47117, '<td valign="top">I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are <br/>near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry <br/>in this challenge.<br/> <br/>This photo is extremely small, and I am sure you got a few of those comments already.  The moment, to me, is really not a good candid one.  It does tell a bit of a story as the boy seems to be reflecting on a moment of his life, but I just don''t find this a top pic for me. Technically, I would have made it large, and toned it to b/w or sepia to give more to the mood.</td>', 'I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry in this challenge. This photo is extremely small, and I am sure you got a few of those comments already.  The moment, to me, is really not a good candid one.  It does tell a bit of a story as the boy seems to be reflecting on a moment of his life, but I just don''t find this a top pic for me. Technically, I would have made it large, and toned it to b/w or sepia to give more to the mood.', '2006-04-18 15:40:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(2322210, 320009, 47117, '<td valign="top">I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are <br/>near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry <br/>in this challenge.<br/> <br/>If I were to list this in categories, it would be under performance and snapshot. The photo is way out of focus aside from the motion blur, and badly lit. Unfortunately I have to say it was badly composed. Not much of interest is being portrayed that isn''t expected.  It''s a 2 for me.</td>', 'I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry in this challenge. If I were to list this in categories, it would be under performance and snapshot. The photo is way out of focus aside from the motion blur, and badly lit. Unfortunately I have to say it was badly composed. Not much of interest is being portrayed that isn''t expected.  It''s a 2 for me.', '2006-04-18 15:40:43.000000', NULL, 1),
