(2323128, 318320, 23394, '<td valign="top">focus is way off.  the subject looks like it could have some potential, and the lighting looks like it could be interesting, but not the way you have it here.  what could be done to make this better?  well, it depends on what you''re trying to do--improve your photography, or improve your dpc scores?  if you want to improve your photography, well, keep working at it.  if you want to show motion, you have to have absolute razor sharp focus with good panning.  if you want to freeze action, you''ll have to bump up your shutter speed to at least 1/250 (as well as have good focus).  compositionally, this is ok, but it would be stronger with the subject''s face, rather than their backside.<br/> <br/>on the other hand, if you''re looking to improve your scores, you might want to read this <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/forum.php?action=read&amp;FORUM_THREAD_ID=156130#1084676" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">thread</a>.</td>', 'focus is way off.  the subject looks like it could have some potential, and the lighting looks like it could be interesting, but not the way you have it here.  what could be done to make this better?  well, it depends on what you''re trying to do--improve your photography, or improve your dpc scores?  if you want to improve your photography, well, keep working at it.  if you want to show motion, you have to have absolute razor sharp focus with good panning.  if you want to freeze action, you''ll have to bump up your shutter speed to at least 1/250 (as well as have good focus).  compositionally, this is ok, but it would be stronger with the subject''s face, rather than their backside. on the other hand, if you''re looking to improve your scores, you might want to read this thread.', '2006-04-18 21:17:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(2323131, 317658, 23394, '<td valign="top">echoing the other probable comments, this image is too small to be voted fairly and/or commented on.  if your score isn''t where you would like it to be, you might want to read this <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/forum.php?action=read&amp;FORUM_THREAD_ID=156130#1084676" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">thread</a>.</td>', 'echoing the other probable comments, this image is too small to be voted fairly and/or commented on.  if your score isn''t where you would like it to be, you might want to read this thread.', '2006-04-18 21:17:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(2323135, 317432, 23394, '<td valign="top">i''m sure there''s a story here somewhere, but you''ve put most of the burden on me and my imagination to draw it out, rather than offering much in the way of imagery.  it''s a guy walking away from me.  nothing of interest to clue me in as to where he''s going or where he''s coming from?  more than likely, you could have gotten a better shot at the bus stop.</td>', 'i''m sure there''s a story here somewhere, but you''ve put most of the burden on me and my imagination to draw it out, rather than offering much in the way of imagery.  it''s a guy walking away from me.  nothing of interest to clue me in as to where he''s going or where he''s coming from?  more than likely, you could have gotten a better shot at the bus stop.', '2006-04-18 21:20:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(2323138, 318844, 23394, '<td valign="top">cute, maybe, but not to me.  there''s just something off about this image.  maybe if you had cropped in tighter to the face, leaving off the hand in motion.  even though the subject is absolutely engrossed in whatever has her attention, you haven''t given me any context for enjoying what''s going on.</td>', 'cute, maybe, but not to me.  there''s just something off about this image.  maybe if you had cropped in tighter to the face, leaving off the hand in motion.  even though the subject is absolutely engrossed in whatever has her attention, you haven''t given me any context for enjoying what''s going on.', '2006-04-18 21:22:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(2323141, 319036, 23394, '<td valign="top">oh, man, i''m sure there''s a story here, but not in the way you''ve presented it.  would love to see the face and its expressions.  as is, you''ve given me a small snapshot of someone you saw on the street, but nothing more that would keep my interest.</td>', 'oh, man, i''m sure there''s a story here, but not in the way you''ve presented it.  would love to see the face and its expressions.  as is, you''ve given me a small snapshot of someone you saw on the street, but nothing more that would keep my interest.', '2006-04-18 21:24:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(2323148, 319904, 23394, '<td valign="top">ay-yi-yi.  yeah, this is a candid opportunity, but how did you shoot it.  this looks like a crop of something you shot from a mile away, under very bad conditions.  i bet if you had approached him and talked with him a moment, you probably could have gotten a fantastic shot, as well as had a meaningful engagement with another human being.  as is, i feel completely isolated from him, like i''m looking at an empty image full of potential.<br/> <br/>(as a side note, when i''m out shooting around, i carry a case of water in the car, not just for me, but also to share with people like this.  you never know who you''re gonna meet or if you can help them, but, all the same, everybody gets thirsty...)</td>', 'ay-yi-yi.  yeah, this is a candid opportunity, but how did you shoot it.  this looks like a crop of something you shot from a mile away, under very bad conditions.  i bet if you had approached him and talked with him a moment, you probably could have gotten a fantastic shot, as well as had a meaningful engagement with another human being.  as is, i feel completely isolated from him, like i''m looking at an empty image full of potential. (as a side note, when i''m out shooting around, i carry a case of water in the car, not just for me, but also to share with people like this.  you never know who you''re gonna meet or if you can help them, but, all the same, everybody gets thirsty...)', '2006-04-18 21:28:46.000000', NULL, 1),
