(2325198, 319760, 21714, '<td valign="top">Congratulations, Ed.<br/>Enjoyed this one.</td>', 'Congratulations, Ed.Enjoyed this one.', '2006-04-19 09:54:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(2325226, 319308, 41504, '<td valign="top">Well, I hardly ever shoot people pics, now I know why.  To those who said it was staged, I can assure you it wasn''t.  I had intentionally framed using the rock and grass to try to show him peaking.  I just caught him as he looked up.  Oh well, on to the next challenge.</td>', 'Well, I hardly ever shoot people pics, now I know why.  To those who said it was staged, I can assure you it wasn''t.  I had intentionally framed using the rock and grass to try to show him peaking.  I just caught him as he looked up.  Oh well, on to the next challenge.', '2006-04-19 10:02:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(2325228, 319760, 36382, '<td valign="top">Congratulations.  This was my fave and it wasn''t just me!</td>', 'Congratulations.  This was my fave and it wasn''t just me!', '2006-04-19 10:02:26.000000', NULL, 0);
INSERT INTO comments ("id", "image_id", "commenter_id", "raw_comment", "comment", "date", "edited", "made_during_challenge") VALUES
(2325333, 317890, 20056, '<td valign="top">Thanks everybody for your comments... I realized after some of them that "candid moments" is not the same as "candid" ... I just followed candid definition which better apply to animals than persons, but definetely candid moments apply more to persons.<br/> <br/>Just, some explanation about the wet fur... it was snowing all the day (You can se the background... all the backyard was very wet.<br/> <br/>By far, my best portrait... ZD 50-200 mm lens are really great!<br/> <br/>Thanks again and have fun shooting! :)</td>', 'Thanks everybody for your comments... I realized after some of them that "candid moments" is not the same as "candid" ... I just followed candid definition which better apply to animals than persons, but definetely candid moments apply more to persons. Just, some explanation about the wet fur... it was snowing all the day (You can se the background... all the backyard was very wet. By far, my best portrait... ZD 50-200 mm lens are really great! Thanks again and have fun shooting! :)', '2006-04-19 10:27:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(2325393, 318058, 42196, '<td valign="top">Excellent expression you''ve captured!<br/> <br/>What was the focal length on this?<br/> <br/></td>', 'Excellent expression you''ve captured! What was the focal length on this? ', '2006-04-19 10:42:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(2325448, 318058, 37893, '<td valign="top">Congrats Frank! This was one of the first images that struck me in the challenge. Great find. Pike Place Market is where I have some of my best candid shots ;)</td>', 'Congrats Frank! This was one of the first images that struck me in the challenge. Great find. Pike Place Market is where I have some of my best candid shots ;)', '2006-04-19 10:59:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(2325462, 318354, 21714, '<td valign="top">This was my favourite in the challenge.<br/>Well done.</td>', 'This was my favourite in the challenge.Well done.', '2006-04-19 11:03:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(2325488, 319760, 5728, '<td valign="top">My favourite shot of the challenge. I am happy it ended up getting a ribbon after all. Respect on such an amazing image Ed!</td>', 'My favourite shot of the challenge. I am happy it ended up getting a ribbon after all. Respect on such an amazing image Ed!', '2006-04-19 11:08:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(2325511, 320025, 6999, '<td valign="top">Man, you got flamed! Whilst I wouldn''t call this completely successful, it certainly doesn''t deserve these ignorant and thoughtless and plain stupid comments - ''rules'' of candids my ****</td>', 'Man, you got flamed! Whilst I wouldn''t call this completely successful, it certainly doesn''t deserve these ignorant and thoughtless and plain stupid comments - ''rules'' of candids my ****', '2006-04-19 11:20:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(2325519, 319295, 21714, '<td valign="top">Since you did know it wouldn''t do well on DPC, I think you have a very clear and good understanding of how things work around here. <br/>I thought it was one of the best in the challenge, and on it''s own a fine image. Well done.</td>', 'Since you did know it wouldn''t do well on DPC, I think you have a very clear and good understanding of how things work around here. I thought it was one of the best in the challenge, and on it''s own a fine image. Well done.', '2006-04-19 11:28:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(2325523, 320029, 26045, '<td valign="top">thanks everyone for the comments :)<br/> <br/>i shouldn''t have entered this one into candids. but, i''ve just stopped caring. bahaha<br/> <br/>i do appreciate all your thoughts, whether or not i agree with them ;)<br/> <br/>earthquake girl, out<br/> <br/></td>', 'thanks everyone for the comments :) i shouldn''t have entered this one into candids. but, i''ve just stopped caring. bahaha i do appreciate all your thoughts, whether or not i agree with them ;) earthquake girl, out ', '2006-04-19 11:29:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(2325528, 318381, 3306, '<td valign="top">Great Capture. Congrats on the top 20.</td>', 'Great Capture. Congrats on the top 20.', '2006-04-19 11:32:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(2325543, 319415, 13390, '<td valign="top">Way to go Jen! This definitely scored much better. Good shot I must say. Just for future reference, you can adjust curves, leves, etc. under the <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/challenge_rules.php?RULES_ID=10" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Basic Editing Rules</a> to help brighten up pictures that are a tad on the darker side. Another cool little tool that most people use that is legal under the basic editing rules is a program called NeatImage. You can download it at www.neatimage.com and you can download the Noise Profile for you specific camera. If you have questions about that program, just do a search in the forums or make a forum post on it. There are a TON of helpful people here. BTW, I hereby challenge you to both the Negative and Complimentary Colors Challenges. Do you accept?</td>', 'Way to go Jen! This definitely scored much better. Good shot I must say. Just for future reference, you can adjust curves, leves, etc. under the Basic Editing Rules to help brighten up pictures that are a tad on the darker side. Another cool little tool that most people use that is legal under the basic editing rules is a program called NeatImage. You can download it at www.neatimage.com and you can download the Noise Profile for you specific camera. If you have questions about that program, just do a search in the forums or make a forum post on it. There are a TON of helpful people here. BTW, I hereby challenge you to both the Negative and Complimentary Colors Challenges. Do you accept?', '2006-04-19 11:41:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(2325544, 319336, 35994, '<td valign="top">This shot shows so much emotion, great candid! Really makes you feel for the man that''s lost someone close to him.</td>', 'This shot shows so much emotion, great candid! Really makes you feel for the man that''s lost someone close to him.', '2006-04-19 11:42:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(2325546, 318058, 34938, '<td valign="top">Congratulations on your second ribbon Frank...well deserved. Gave you an 8...wish I gave you 10. Great work.</td>', 'Congratulations on your second ribbon Frank...well deserved. Gave you an 8...wish I gave you 10. Great work.', '2006-04-19 11:43:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(2325550, 319581, 34938, '<td valign="top">Yo Rikki...congratulations on your 5th spot. What a wonderful shot! You are a gun!</td>', 'Yo Rikki...congratulations on your 5th spot. What a wonderful shot! You are a gun!', '2006-04-19 11:44:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(2325552, 319295, 14620, '<td valign="top">You were "forced" to go to a bar eh? :-)  Sad to see this so low but glad you entered it.</td>', 'You were "forced" to go to a bar eh? :-)  Sad to see this so low but glad you entered it.', '2006-04-19 11:45:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(2325557, 319389, 13390, '<td valign="top">Congratulations on your first entry! You even did better than me on your first entry than I did on mine! I would definitely echo what was said about making the crop a little bit tighter to emphasize the embrace. There''s just a tadd too much negative space on the bottom and detracts the eye from the intended subject and causes he ye to wander a bit. I realize that the S7000 uses a 4:3 ratio crop. With this shot I probably would have usd the traditional 3:2 ratio and cut off a little bit of the bottom. I think it might have helped to get a little more of the brides head in there, that may have also put the hands at one of the Rule of 3rds intersections. Hope that helps! Looking good! I look forward to your future entries.</td>', 'Congratulations on your first entry! You even did better than me on your first entry than I did on mine! I would definitely echo what was said about making the crop a little bit tighter to emphasize the embrace. There''s just a tadd too much negative space on the bottom and detracts the eye from the intended subject and causes he ye to wander a bit. I realize that the S7000 uses a 4:3 ratio crop. With this shot I probably would have usd the traditional 3:2 ratio and cut off a little bit of the bottom. I think it might have helped to get a little more of the brides head in there, that may have also put the hands at one of the Rule of 3rds intersections. Hope that helps! Looking good! I look forward to your future entries.', '2006-04-19 11:47:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(2325566, 318904, 48298, '<td valign="top">Sheesh...people were tough on you on this one.<br/>Hey, you got a couple of nines and tens, though!<br/>Well, they said Candid, and it is Candid, so smile.<br/>Don''t feel bad.  Looks like you were having fun, and at least you have friends!  :)<br/></td>', 'Sheesh...people were tough on you on this one.Hey, you got a couple of nines and tens, though!Well, they said Candid, and it is Candid, so smile.Don''t feel bad.  Looks like you were having fun, and at least you have friends!  :)', '2006-04-19 11:53:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(2325569, 318058, 15711, '<td valign="top">Such a fun shot. Congrats.</td>', 'Such a fun shot. Congrats.', '2006-04-19 11:54:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(2325590, 319535, 32767, '<td valign="top">I gave you a 4 and now that I look at the image again...No Offense...I''m surprised I gave it that high a score. Generally speaking technicals aren''t the most important thing when it comes to Candids but the better the technicals the cooler the shot...that''s to say, if the techs are off, it had better be a damn cool moment that you''ve captured.<br/> <br/>Great techs means you were quick and nailed it on the money...when it counted. There is some major blowouts in your image, the coloring is drab and the focus isn''t really on.<br/> <br/>Now this is a picture of a Swan swimming by some weeds...no special or intersting action or moment to speak of (fishing, being attacked...making whoopeee)...though yes, it was of course a moment in time. Sure it''s a Candid but a Candid of something with virtually no interest. Basically this image has more issues than just the fact that it was an animal Candid.<br/> <br/>My comments are pretty stiff because I''m at work and don''t have the time to edit my thoughts but since you started a thread I figured I''d give you both barrels while have the energy to be honest. No offense please.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-04-19 18:42:21.</i></td>', 'I gave you a 4 and now that I look at the image again...No Offense...I''m surprised I gave it that high a score. Generally speaking technicals aren''t the most important thing when it comes to Candids but the better the technicals the cooler the shot...that''s to say, if the techs are off, it had better be a damn cool moment that you''ve captured. Great techs means you were quick and nailed it on the money...when it counted. There is some major blowouts in your image, the coloring is drab and the focus isn''t really on. Now this is a picture of a Swan swimming by some weeds...no special or intersting action or moment to speak of (fishing, being attacked...making whoopeee)...though yes, it was of course a moment in time. Sure it''s a Candid but a Candid of something with virtually no interest. Basically this image has more issues than just the fact that it was an animal Candid. My comments are pretty stiff because I''m at work and don''t have the time to edit my thoughts but since you started a thread I figured I''d give you both barrels while have the energy to be honest. No offense please.', '2006-04-19 12:02:39.000000', '2006-04-19 19:42:21.000000', 0),
(2325591, 319295, 15711, '<td valign="top">I really like this, but lately, what I enter and like isn''t doing so well. The movement is great.  Has a photojournalism quality. Too bad others don''t get it, huh?</td>', 'I really like this, but lately, what I enter and like isn''t doing so well. The movement is great.  Has a photojournalism quality. Too bad others don''t get it, huh?', '2006-04-19 12:02:49.000000', NULL, 0),
