(2325775, 318516, 51939, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by espy:</b></div><hr/><i> I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are <br/>near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry <br/>in this challenge.<br/> <br/>A pretty color portrait, but by far anythign from a candid in my book. Good dof. The lighting could be better, but she is obviously looking straight into and at the camera and the photographer. Cute little girl though, just not a good entry for this challenge. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks for the feedback.  Just beginning to take a long time interest (photography) seriously and value all the input I can get.  Your right about it not really being a candid.  I was so excited about a new camera and posting a pic for the contest the I missed one most important details.<br/>J</td>', 'Originally posted by espy: I''m not much for receiving or giving comments, but since Candids are near and dear to my heart, I have decided to give comment on every entry in this challenge. A pretty color portrait, but by far anythign from a candid in my book. Good dof. The lighting could be better, but she is obviously looking straight into and at the camera and the photographer. Cute little girl though, just not a good entry for this challenge.   Thanks for the feedback.  Just beginning to take a long time interest (photography) seriously and value all the input I can get.  Your right about it not really being a candid.  I was so excited about a new camera and posting a pic for the contest the I missed one most important details.J', '2006-04-19 13:13:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(2325783, 318058, 16046, '<td valign="top">Hey cool, I was worried with all the other fine entries that I would place in the top 10. Once again, tough compition. If you ever go to the Pike Place Market in Seattle, you might see this guy singing with 3 or 4 others in front of the original Starbucks store. Worth the listen. Here''s my outtake, my family picked the winner over this one;<br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=323362" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/16046/thumb/323362.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/16046/thumb/323362.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/16046/thumb/323362.jpg"/></a> <br/>I shot both of these extended out to 200mm w/circular polarizer, which is why I had to boost my ISO up to 640.<br/>Thanks everyone for all the great comments.</td>', 'Hey cool, I was worried with all the other fine entries that I would place in the top 10. Once again, tough compition. If you ever go to the Pike Place Market in Seattle, you might see this guy singing with 3 or 4 others in front of the original Starbucks store. Worth the listen. Here''s my outtake, my family picked the winner over this one; I shot both of these extended out to 200mm w/circular polarizer, which is why I had to boost my ISO up to 640.Thanks everyone for all the great comments.', '2006-04-19 13:15:55.000000', NULL, 0),
