(2326008, 319927, 30982, '<td valign="top">I think this has very good potential, particularly with the way she''s framed by the structure in the background.  As I''m sure others have probably already commented, you needed to have the focus more on your subject than on the traffic.  The look on her face makes the shot.</td>', 'I think this has very good potential, particularly with the way she''s framed by the structure in the background.  As I''m sure others have probably already commented, you needed to have the focus more on your subject than on the traffic.  The look on her face makes the shot.', '2006-04-19 14:24:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(2326030, 319760, 23913, '<td valign="top">just found out the other day dude to a thread that you are one of my statistical favs. lol i gess i know why after seeing this in the challenge it was a fav. right off the bat.<br/> <br/>the moment holds so much its can truly be said that you picture is worth well over a thousand words.<br/> <br/>and i am so glad to see it hit top 3 i truly think it is deserving of 1st but the cards fell as they did eh''.<br/> <br/>anyhow couldn''t let it pass off the front page with out telling you just how truly classic and great this image is. the only way i can really put it is-<br/> <br/>you know those classic photo books the ones with Brasson, and Mark and such? well this is of that grade and if they ever re-publish the time life book of photography series, this image should be in it.<br/> <br/>editing or no Brasson is smiling somewhere just after seeing the look on the face of the Butcher.<br/> <br/>truly a fav.</td>', 'just found out the other day dude to a thread that you are one of my statistical favs. lol i gess i know why after seeing this in the challenge it was a fav. right off the bat. the moment holds so much its can truly be said that you picture is worth well over a thousand words. and i am so glad to see it hit top 3 i truly think it is deserving of 1st but the cards fell as they did eh''. anyhow couldn''t let it pass off the front page with out telling you just how truly classic and great this image is. the only way i can really put it is- you know those classic photo books the ones with Brasson, and Mark and such? well this is of that grade and if they ever re-publish the time life book of photography series, this image should be in it. editing or no Brasson is smiling somewhere just after seeing the look on the face of the Butcher. truly a fav.', '2006-04-19 14:30:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(2326042, 319215, 43150, '<td valign="top">I didn''t vote but i think some people owe this man an Apology! It is very different to think that this photo doesn''t fit the challenge or that it was a bad pic...it is another thing to vote down because of what you think the photo is...we are judging photos not politics.</td>', 'I didn''t vote but i think some people owe this man an Apology! It is very different to think that this photo doesn''t fit the challenge or that it was a bad pic...it is another thing to vote down because of what you think the photo is...we are judging photos not politics.', '2006-04-19 14:34:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(2326059, 319316, 30982, '<td valign="top">Sandy - your people pictures are always wonderful.  The lighting, the color, the clarity are all above average for a candid shot, and those eyes REALLY get your attention!  Nice work, as usual!</td>', 'Sandy - your people pictures are always wonderful.  The lighting, the color, the clarity are all above average for a candid shot, and those eyes REALLY get your attention!  Nice work, as usual!', '2006-04-19 14:41:52.000000', NULL, 0),
