(2326947, 319808, 49973, '<td valign="top">Thanks Melismatica. I am glad you made the observations about them as a couple...pretty accurate.  I also disagree with some of the comments but found the tips helpful which is why I enter these competitions.  i also like to add a bit of humour as some of the entries are a bit stale and far too serious.</td>', 'Thanks Melismatica. I am glad you made the observations about them as a couple...pretty accurate.  I also disagree with some of the comments but found the tips helpful which is why I enter these competitions.  i also like to add a bit of humour as some of the entries are a bit stale and far too serious.', '2006-04-19 18:53:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(2326952, 319760, 30364, '<td valign="top">Back to say I can''t believe nobody has remarked on the wonderful name of the butchery!<br/>Such a wonderful, sly little juxtaposition all of its own, given the prim ''spit and polish'' nature of the butcher.<br/> <br/>The photograph looks like a still from a ''60''s BBC television series, especially as the two main players bring to my mind a couple of characters from that place and time ... the butcher as Captain Peacock (''Are You Being Served?") and the shopper as Captain Mainwaring (''Dad''s Army'').</td>', 'Back to say I can''t believe nobody has remarked on the wonderful name of the butchery!Such a wonderful, sly little juxtaposition all of its own, given the prim ''spit and polish'' nature of the butcher. The photograph looks like a still from a ''60''s BBC television series, especially as the two main players bring to my mind a couple of characters from that place and time ... the butcher as Captain Peacock (''Are You Being Served?") and the shopper as Captain Mainwaring (''Dad''s Army'').', '2006-04-19 18:54:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(2327019, 318501, 14620, '<td valign="top">I''m sure her and her mom would have LOVED a copy of this.</td>', 'I''m sure her and her mom would have LOVED a copy of this.', '2006-04-19 19:29:19.000000', NULL, 0),
