(2328454, 320008, 18450, '<td valign="top">Composition and emotion in this shot are awesome. The expressiveness and direct look in his eyes are classic. Agree with Amy.....would be cool to see it processed w/out the NI.</td>', 'Composition and emotion in this shot are awesome. The expressiveness and direct look in his eyes are classic. Agree with Amy.....would be cool to see it processed w/out the NI.', '2006-04-20 03:26:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(2328524, 319295, 5728, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Ennil:</b></div><hr/><i> Sleezy turkish bar ey? I''ll see you when you come here... You''ll have to be careful what you''re gonna eat with me! <br/> <br/>You''re probably right but still, you struck a cord :P <br/> <br/>Sleezy... ah! And you think your german bars are better! (This would sound so cool with a heavy russian accent :P)<br/> <br/>On another note, I love the pic. Very nice B&amp;W </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>There is an area in Munich called "Little Istanbul". There is also a little red light district in that area and some of the pubs are not really places that I would like to take my mum too :) This was one of them, it just happened to be Turkish, I think next door there was a Bulgarian one or something. After taking photos I bought all these guys at the table a round of beer, and got talking to them a while. Very friendly people you Turks. But the bar was still sleezy :)</td>', 'Originally posted by Ennil: Sleezy turkish bar ey? I''ll see you when you come here... You''ll have to be careful what you''re gonna eat with me!  You''re probably right but still, you struck a cord :P  Sleezy... ah! And you think your german bars are better! (This would sound so cool with a heavy russian accent :P) On another note, I love the pic. Very nice B&W   There is an area in Munich called "Little Istanbul". There is also a little red light district in that area and some of the pubs are not really places that I would like to take my mum too :) This was one of them, it just happened to be Turkish, I think next door there was a Bulgarian one or something. After taking photos I bought all these guys at the table a round of beer, and got talking to them a while. Very friendly people you Turks. But the bar was still sleezy :)', '2006-04-20 04:29:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(2328554, 319760, 6999, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by internationalmanofmystery:</b></div><hr/><i> Lots of character in this shot. I like it and I think it deserved to come 1st! Incidentally, isn''t it against EU law to advertise in lb rather than kg? :) </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>That''s it! But if I''d called it ''The EU commissioner of weights and measures comes to visit'' I think fewer people would have liked it. And Martin - Shambles as in the famous street in York (actually the cross-street at the end of the shot) but your point is well made.</td>', 'Originally posted by internationalmanofmystery: Lots of character in this shot. I like it and I think it deserved to come 1st! Incidentally, isn''t it against EU law to advertise in lb rather than kg? :)   That''s it! But if I''d called it ''The EU commissioner of weights and measures comes to visit'' I think fewer people would have liked it. And Martin - Shambles as in the famous street in York (actually the cross-street at the end of the shot) but your point is well made.', '2006-04-20 04:56:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(2328589, 319002, 22301, '<td valign="top">Can i add comments to my own pictures?</td>', 'Can i add comments to my own pictures?', '2006-04-20 05:33:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(2328664, 317746, 6999, '<td valign="top">People''s attitudes to a repeating subject are interesting, aren''t they? Stylistically, this is very different from what we know as a ''librodo'' look, and yet it seems to me there is more attention paid to the model than the photography here. It''s a grand shot, and she has an amazing face, but perhaps people were looking for something more ... active, perhaps - interactive maybe. Maybe it''s too close to folks'' idea of a ''portrait''. All the usual DPC imponderables :-)</td>', 'People''s attitudes to a repeating subject are interesting, aren''t they? Stylistically, this is very different from what we know as a ''librodo'' look, and yet it seems to me there is more attention paid to the model than the photography here. It''s a grand shot, and she has an amazing face, but perhaps people were looking for something more ... active, perhaps - interactive maybe. Maybe it''s too close to folks'' idea of a ''portrait''. All the usual DPC imponderables :-)', '2006-04-20 06:52:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(2328729, 319839, 39850, '<td valign="top">I gave this a 6.  Thought you captured a candid moment quite well.  Colors were good.  A little more defined on the boy''s face, but difficult with a candid - especially after having read your comment that he was waving to his younger brother, which by the way, I didn''t notice the ''wave'' during the ''brief voting/viewing'' I did do - just thought it was a ''hand movement'' of sorts.  Perhaps a tighter cropping on the right may have accentuated that, as the girl in the rear, although adds something, draws attention away from him slightly, in my opinion.  Of course, the ''younger brother'' in frame would have been good but I''m sure you''d have included that if you had it.</td>', 'I gave this a 6.  Thought you captured a candid moment quite well.  Colors were good.  A little more defined on the boy''s face, but difficult with a candid - especially after having read your comment that he was waving to his younger brother, which by the way, I didn''t notice the ''wave'' during the ''brief voting/viewing'' I did do - just thought it was a ''hand movement'' of sorts.  Perhaps a tighter cropping on the right may have accentuated that, as the girl in the rear, although adds something, draws attention away from him slightly, in my opinion.  Of course, the ''younger brother'' in frame would have been good but I''m sure you''d have included that if you had it.', '2006-04-20 07:33:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(2328761, 320008, 30454, '<td valign="top">Thanks everyone for your comments. Here is the less "plastic" version. Hope you will like it.<br/> <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=323509" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/30454/thumb/323509.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/30454/thumb/323509.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/30454/thumb/323509.jpg"/></a><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-04-20 07:30:55.</i></td>', 'Thanks everyone for your comments. Here is the less "plastic" version. Hope you will like it. ', '2006-04-20 08:30:41.000000', '2006-04-20 08:30:55.000000', 0),
(2328771, 318501, 27475, '<td valign="top">This pic is amaizing, not only for the quality, but the story behind.<br/>She looks like a fighter, and the look in her eye is so much older that it should be and it''s so contradicting with the Cirque du Soleil painting she has.<br/> <br/>Congrads and good luck to her and her family.<br/> <br/>Think there''s any way of getting this picture to here and her family?</td>', 'This pic is amaizing, not only for the quality, but the story behind.She looks like a fighter, and the look in her eye is so much older that it should be and it''s so contradicting with the Cirque du Soleil painting she has. Congrads and good luck to her and her family. Think there''s any way of getting this picture to here and her family?', '2006-04-20 08:39:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(2328864, 319760, 30861, '<td valign="top">Ed, I''m just getting caught up on this challenge. Marvelous entry, but even MORE marvelous is the lovely story you appended to the comments section. Very Holmesian deductions, I rather fancy... Great job!</td>', 'Ed, I''m just getting caught up on this challenge. Marvelous entry, but even MORE marvelous is the lovely story you appended to the comments section. Very Holmesian deductions, I rather fancy... Great job!', '2006-04-20 09:40:59.000000', NULL, 0),
