(2338298, 318501, 18339, '<td valign="top">What a beautiful story behind this picture.  I was at festival and know the hair booth youre talking about. It really touches my heart to visualize this scene and the air brush artist being sensitive enough to make her feel special.  Congratulations on a well deserved top 10.  Incredible portrait.</td>', 'What a beautiful story behind this picture.  I was at festival and know the hair booth youre talking about. It really touches my heart to visualize this scene and the air brush artist being sensitive enough to make her feel special.  Congratulations on a well deserved top 10.  Incredible portrait.', '2006-04-24 03:33:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(2338356, 320040, 43434, '<td valign="top"><b><i>::: Critique Club :::</i></b> <br/> <br/>Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club.<br/> <br/>Interesting to do a critique on your image but it is difficult if you don''t give us any information in your photographers comments.  When we do a critique, we go past just the photographic result, that''s what voters comments do.  The critique looks at what you were trying to achieve, how you wanted it to look and what issues you had in getting the image captured and ready for voting.<br/> <br/><b>First Impression - the most important one:</b> <br/>Lovely stop motion with the water ... good looking kiddy with great taste in hats.<br/> <br/><b>Composition:</b> <br/>This works well ... I also like the reflection in the tap.<br/> <br/><b>Subject:</b> <br/>meets the challenge well .. although she does appear to be watching you ..that just means she is an aware kid.<br/> <br/><b>Technical (Colour and light):</b> <br/>Sorry but I don''t really know what you are aiming for with no photog.s comments.  This is sharp and well processed.<br/> <br/><b>To grow its vote?:</b> <br/>Candids are hard and something that needs time and patience .. and practice .. .you are doing well.<br/> <br/><b>Summary:</b> <br/>Great shot ... well done .. .can''t wait to see more.<br/> <br/>If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via the PM system.<br/> <br/>Cheers<br/> <br/>Kari</td>', '::: Critique Club :::  Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club. Interesting to do a critique on your image but it is difficult if you don''t give us any information in your photographers comments.  When we do a critique, we go past just the photographic result, that''s what voters comments do.  The critique looks at what you were trying to achieve, how you wanted it to look and what issues you had in getting the image captured and ready for voting. First Impression - the most important one: Lovely stop motion with the water ... good looking kiddy with great taste in hats. Composition: This works well ... I also like the reflection in the tap. Subject: meets the challenge well .. although she does appear to be watching you ..that just means she is an aware kid. Technical (Colour and light): Sorry but I don''t really know what you are aiming for with no photog.s comments.  This is sharp and well processed. To grow its vote?: Candids are hard and something that needs time and patience .. and practice .. .you are doing well. Summary: Great shot ... well done .. .can''t wait to see more. If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via the PM system. Cheers Kari', '2006-04-24 04:35:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(2338360, 319751, 43434, '<td valign="top"><b><i>::: Critique Club :::</i></b> <br/> <br/>Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club.<br/> <br/>Interesting to do a critique on your image but it is difficult if you don''t give us any information in your photographers comments.  When we do a critique, we go past just the photographic result, that''s what voters comments do.  The critique looks at what you were trying to achieve, how you wanted it to look and what issues you had in getting the image captured and ready for voting.<br/> <br/><b>First Impression - the most important one:</b> <br/>This is a good candid ... he looks interesting and it tells a story.<br/> <br/><b>Composition:</b> <br/>Interesting lines created with this image ... maybe the background a minor issue .. but hey its a candid .. so what can you do!<br/> <br/><b>Subject:</b> <br/>Meets and excels at this challenge.<br/> <br/><b>Technical (Colour and light):</b> <br/>Good natural colours .. and a sharp picture.<br/> <br/><b>To grow its vote?:</b> <br/>You did great in this challenge ... to get where you did ... and to get the meaning of what a candid is ... just keep practicing Candids are the hardest pics to pull off ..<br/> <br/><b>Summary:</b> <br/>This is great ... keep it up you are building a great portfolio ... all the best.<br/> <br/>If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via the PM system.<br/> <br/>Cheers<br/> <br/>Kari</td>', '::: Critique Club :::  Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club. Interesting to do a critique on your image but it is difficult if you don''t give us any information in your photographers comments.  When we do a critique, we go past just the photographic result, that''s what voters comments do.  The critique looks at what you were trying to achieve, how you wanted it to look and what issues you had in getting the image captured and ready for voting. First Impression - the most important one: This is a good candid ... he looks interesting and it tells a story. Composition: Interesting lines created with this image ... maybe the background a minor issue .. but hey its a candid .. so what can you do! Subject: Meets and excels at this challenge. Technical (Colour and light): Good natural colours .. and a sharp picture. To grow its vote?: You did great in this challenge ... to get where you did ... and to get the meaning of what a candid is ... just keep practicing Candids are the hardest pics to pull off .. Summary: This is great ... keep it up you are building a great portfolio ... all the best. If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via the PM system. Cheers Kari', '2006-04-24 04:41:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(2338367, 319985, 43434, '<td valign="top"><b><i>::: Critique Club :::</i></b> <br/> <br/>Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club.<br/> <br/>WOW first submission .. try to make this painless!<br/> <br/><b>First Impression - the most important one:</b> <br/>I love this shot ... it is a unique way od doing a candid ... It is amazing what people take offence to ... so suck it in and see :)<br/> <br/><b>Composition:</b> <br/>I really like the balance of this shot ... The lines in this shot work really well ... <br/> <br/><b>Subject:</b> <br/>Meets the challenge well ... he really doesn''t know you are there ... good shot!<br/> <br/><b>Technical (Colour and light):</b> <br/>Hard to comment colour on a black and white .. but this is NOT a black and white overkill it really does suit this shot.  I like the natural lighting ... Agree with the minor reduction in brightness ..I often do this and upping the contrast just brings out clear lines.  I think that mentioned in the comments is that one commentor wanted to see more of the pictures .. this is probably in the DOF you used .. I think that this worked as it was.<br/> <br/><b>To grow its vote?:</b> <br/>Every way is up ... this is your first challenge I expect good things ... think about all the rules .. you will learn them at DPC ... and take in the many positve comments you receive ... remember to filter what you hear - no one is perfect!<br/> <br/><b>Summary:</b> <br/>5.259 173 / 393 56% for a first entry ... keep this up!  You are good!<br/> <br/>If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via the PM system.<br/> <br/>Cheers<br/> <br/>Kari</td>', '::: Critique Club :::  Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club. WOW first submission .. try to make this painless! First Impression - the most important one: I love this shot ... it is a unique way od doing a candid ... It is amazing what people take offence to ... so suck it in and see :) Composition: I really like the balance of this shot ... The lines in this shot work really well ...  Subject: Meets the challenge well ... he really doesn''t know you are there ... good shot! Technical (Colour and light): Hard to comment colour on a black and white .. but this is NOT a black and white overkill it really does suit this shot.  I like the natural lighting ... Agree with the minor reduction in brightness ..I often do this and upping the contrast just brings out clear lines.  I think that mentioned in the comments is that one commentor wanted to see more of the pictures .. this is probably in the DOF you used .. I think that this worked as it was. To grow its vote?: Every way is up ... this is your first challenge I expect good things ... think about all the rules .. you will learn them at DPC ... and take in the many positve comments you receive ... remember to filter what you hear - no one is perfect! Summary: 5.259 173 / 393 56% for a first entry ... keep this up!  You are good! If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via the PM system. Cheers Kari', '2006-04-24 04:48:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(2338378, 319813, 43434, '<td valign="top"><b><i>::: Critique Club :::</i></b> <br/> <br/>Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club.<br/> <br/>Interesting to do a critique on your image but it is difficult if you don''t give us any information in your photographers comments.  When we do a critique, we go past just the photographic result, that''s what voters comments do.  The critique looks at what you were trying to achieve, how you wanted it to look and what issues you had in getting the image captured and ready for voting.<br/> <br/><b>First Impression - the most important one:</b> <br/>The title gives it a lot ... but the picture is really quite a good candid .. I doubt she would be that happy to have people thinking she has fleas! ... <br/> <br/><b>Composition:</b> <br/>This is not a bad shot and not a bad crop .. but it feels to me like  little like something is missing ... maybe a slightly squarer crop may have worked .. with more of her ... not sure ... just keep trying and seeing what you think ...<br/> <br/><b>Subject:</b> <br/>Meets the challenge .. .and your commentors think so too ... "Animal rights activists acting like animals?"<br/> <br/><b>Technical (Colour and light):</b> <br/>This is fine ... I was thinking maybe the black and white is a little overkill with this shot .. It would be nice to see some colour and pinkness in her cheeks I guess ..<br/> <br/><b>To grow its vote?:</b> <br/>Think hard about the choice of black and white in your entries . .sometimes it works and others it doesn''t ,.. I am not sure which it is here .. Personally only I would love to see in colour ... (that is a personal thought only)<br/> <br/><b>Summary:</b> <br/>I think this is a good solid shot .. and you are improving all the time .. keep it up.<br/> <br/>If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via the PM system.<br/> <br/>Cheers<br/> <br/>Kari</td>', '::: Critique Club :::  Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club. Interesting to do a critique on your image but it is difficult if you don''t give us any information in your photographers comments.  When we do a critique, we go past just the photographic result, that''s what voters comments do.  The critique looks at what you were trying to achieve, how you wanted it to look and what issues you had in getting the image captured and ready for voting. First Impression - the most important one: The title gives it a lot ... but the picture is really quite a good candid .. I doubt she would be that happy to have people thinking she has fleas! ...  Composition: This is not a bad shot and not a bad crop .. but it feels to me like  little like something is missing ... maybe a slightly squarer crop may have worked .. with more of her ... not sure ... just keep trying and seeing what you think ... Subject: Meets the challenge .. .and your commentors think so too ... "Animal rights activists acting like animals?" Technical (Colour and light): This is fine ... I was thinking maybe the black and white is a little overkill with this shot .. It would be nice to see some colour and pinkness in her cheeks I guess .. To grow its vote?: Think hard about the choice of black and white in your entries . .sometimes it works and others it doesn''t ,.. I am not sure which it is here .. Personally only I would love to see in colour ... (that is a personal thought only) Summary: I think this is a good solid shot .. and you are improving all the time .. keep it up. If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via the PM system. Cheers Kari', '2006-04-24 05:00:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(2338393, 319523, 43434, '<td valign="top"><b><i>::: Critique Club :::</i></b> <br/> <br/>Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club.  I think this is the first critique you have had.  I noticed that you never include photographers comments and on this I think that you should know that it is difficult if you don''t give us any information in your photographers comments.  <br/> <br/>When we do a critique, we go past just the photographic result, that''s what voters comments do.  The critique looks at what you were trying to achieve, how you wanted it to look and what issues you had in getting the image captured and ready for voting.<br/> <br/><b>First Impression - the most important one:</b> <br/>Definately looks candid ... she has one whooper of a camera.<br/> <br/><b>Composition:</b> <br/>A little cut short on the left side of the picture for me ... I think it may have worked better with her body playing along the vertical thirds line just to make her the focus of the picture and remove it from the picture she is taking. <br/> <br/><b>Subject:</b> <br/>This seems to meet the challenge well ... congrats on that .. candids are really hard to do.  Maybe others felt that it was posed and that is why the scores of ones .. I am noat sure.<br/> <br/><b>Technical (Colour and light):</b> <br/>Would love to see the richness of the colours in the sorroundings she is in ... the DOF seems to work well here ... but it really does seem a little black and white overkill.<br/> <br/><b>To grow its vote?:</b> <br/>Try it in colour and some different crops ... to see how they work.<br/> <br/><b>Summary:</b> <br/>Good solid shot .. well done, keep shooting as you are doing really well.<br/> <br/>If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via the PM system.<br/> <br/>Cheers<br/> <br/>Kari</td>', '::: Critique Club :::  Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club.  I think this is the first critique you have had.  I noticed that you never include photographers comments and on this I think that you should know that it is difficult if you don''t give us any information in your photographers comments.   When we do a critique, we go past just the photographic result, that''s what voters comments do.  The critique looks at what you were trying to achieve, how you wanted it to look and what issues you had in getting the image captured and ready for voting. First Impression - the most important one: Definately looks candid ... she has one whooper of a camera. Composition: A little cut short on the left side of the picture for me ... I think it may have worked better with her body playing along the vertical thirds line just to make her the focus of the picture and remove it from the picture she is taking.  Subject: This seems to meet the challenge well ... congrats on that .. candids are really hard to do.  Maybe others felt that it was posed and that is why the scores of ones .. I am noat sure. Technical (Colour and light): Would love to see the richness of the colours in the sorroundings she is in ... the DOF seems to work well here ... but it really does seem a little black and white overkill. To grow its vote?: Try it in colour and some different crops ... to see how they work. Summary: Good solid shot .. well done, keep shooting as you are doing really well. If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via the PM system. Cheers Kari', '2006-04-24 05:32:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(2338397, 318095, 43434, '<td valign="top"><b><i>::: Critique Club :::</i></b> <br/> <br/>Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club.<br/> <br/>Interesting to do a critique on your image but it is difficult if you don''t give us any information in your photographers comments.  When we do a critique, we go past just the photographic result, that''s what voters comments do.  The critique looks at what you were trying to achieve, how you wanted it to look and what issues you had in getting the image captured and ready for voting.<br/> <br/><b>First Impression - the most important one:</b> <br/>This is a wonderful shot .. but not a candid (this seems to come through in the comments you received but you do not refute in your photographers comments so that is what I need to look at).<br/> <br/><b>Composition:</b> <br/>Lovely ... for a portrait this would have done really well.<br/> <br/><b>Subject:</b> <br/>Does not meet the challenge .. so is well off subject .. doesn''t mean it ain''t good.<br/> <br/><b>Technical (Colour and light):</b> <br/>Good ... maybe a little oversharpened ... not sure if there is neatimage used or not.<br/> <br/><b>To grow its vote?:</b> <br/>Meet the challenge .. it helps .. and in this case it would have .... as I said it is still a great shot ... <br/> <br/><b>Summary:</b> <br/>You are doing good.  This is a show of good things to come .. keep it up.<br/> <br/>If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via the PM system.<br/> <br/>Cheers<br/> <br/>Kari</td>', '::: Critique Club :::  Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club. Interesting to do a critique on your image but it is difficult if you don''t give us any information in your photographers comments.  When we do a critique, we go past just the photographic result, that''s what voters comments do.  The critique looks at what you were trying to achieve, how you wanted it to look and what issues you had in getting the image captured and ready for voting. First Impression - the most important one: This is a wonderful shot .. but not a candid (this seems to come through in the comments you received but you do not refute in your photographers comments so that is what I need to look at). Composition: Lovely ... for a portrait this would have done really well. Subject: Does not meet the challenge .. so is well off subject .. doesn''t mean it ain''t good. Technical (Colour and light): Good ... maybe a little oversharpened ... not sure if there is neatimage used or not. To grow its vote?: Meet the challenge .. it helps .. and in this case it would have .... as I said it is still a great shot ...  Summary: You are doing good.  This is a show of good things to come .. keep it up. If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via the PM system. Cheers Kari', '2006-04-24 05:37:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(2338415, 319102, 43434, '<td valign="top"><b><i>::: Critique Club :::</i></b> <br/> <br/>Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club.<br/> <br/><b>First Impression - the most important one:</b> <br/>This just drags real emotion ... it is one of those shots it appears, that one either loves or hates.  As shown by the scoring you have both of those extremes in excess.<br/> <br/><b>Composition:</b> <br/>I really like the use of the crop to play the rule of thirds ... The way that the memorial just plays those lines is great.<br/> <br/><b>Subject:</b> <br/>meets the challenge but some may think it doesn''t because the person is hard to make out ... <br/> <br/><b>Technical (Colour and light):</b> <br/>I love this ... you have no issues to me here.<br/> <br/><b>To grow its vote?:</b> <br/>Well you certainly challenged the voters here ... take a safe shot and you will get a higher score .. .but I think sticking outside the small box suits you fine.<br/> <br/><b>Summary:</b> <br/>Wondeful shot .. .for a second challenge entry this tells me you are defiantely on the rise here.<br/> <br/>If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via the PM system.<br/> <br/>Cheers<br/> <br/>Kari</td>', '::: Critique Club :::  Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club. First Impression - the most important one: This just drags real emotion ... it is one of those shots it appears, that one either loves or hates.  As shown by the scoring you have both of those extremes in excess. Composition: I really like the use of the crop to play the rule of thirds ... The way that the memorial just plays those lines is great. Subject: meets the challenge but some may think it doesn''t because the person is hard to make out ...  Technical (Colour and light): I love this ... you have no issues to me here. To grow its vote?: Well you certainly challenged the voters here ... take a safe shot and you will get a higher score .. .but I think sticking outside the small box suits you fine. Summary: Wondeful shot .. .for a second challenge entry this tells me you are defiantely on the rise here. If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via the PM system. Cheers Kari', '2006-04-24 05:52:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(2338423, 319944, 43434, '<td valign="top"><b><i>::: Critique Club :::</i></b> <br/> <br/>Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club.<br/> <br/><b>First Impression - the most important one:</b> <br/>Is an interesting composition ... but doesn''t really meet the challenge ... don''t let that stop you from entering again ... <br/> <br/><b>Composition:</b> <br/>I would like to see more of the person ... just a bit more face from behind the tree (that is if it was a portrait type) ... in a candid this you can''t often control.  This is an interesint crop but it feels like the tree is a barrier.<br/> <br/><b>Subject:</b> <br/>Does not seem to meet the challenge.  but that ain''t the be all and end all of life really.<br/> <br/><b>Technical (Colour and light):</b> <br/>I am one of the people who loves colour when it comes to shots taken in nature ... here the black and white seems a little much .. it works but I think colour would help.<br/> <br/><b>To grow its vote?:</b> <br/>Well meeting the challenge helps .. if you have not sure about how to chekc the forums ..poeple quite often discuss the challenges in the week of entry.<br/> <br/><b>Summary:</b> <br/>Lovely shot ... will be looking for more from you!<br/> <br/>If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via the PM system.<br/> <br/>Cheers<br/> <br/>Kari</td>', '::: Critique Club :::  Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club. First Impression - the most important one: Is an interesting composition ... but doesn''t really meet the challenge ... don''t let that stop you from entering again ...  Composition: I would like to see more of the person ... just a bit more face from behind the tree (that is if it was a portrait type) ... in a candid this you can''t often control.  This is an interesint crop but it feels like the tree is a barrier. Subject: Does not seem to meet the challenge.  but that ain''t the be all and end all of life really. Technical (Colour and light): I am one of the people who loves colour when it comes to shots taken in nature ... here the black and white seems a little much .. it works but I think colour would help. To grow its vote?: Well meeting the challenge helps .. if you have not sure about how to chekc the forums ..poeple quite often discuss the challenges in the week of entry. Summary: Lovely shot ... will be looking for more from you! If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via the PM system. Cheers Kari', '2006-04-24 05:57:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(2338439, 319919, 43434, '<td valign="top"><b><i>::: Critique Club :::</i></b> <br/> <br/>Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club.<br/> <br/><b>First Impression - the most important one:</b> <br/>My dad types like this .. it is cuter when this little one does it!!<br/> <br/><b>Composition:</b> <br/>This is a really well balanced shot and the reflections from the screen are just magic against her face.<br/> <br/><b>Subject:</b> <br/>Meets the challenge to me .. to some it doesn''t ... but kids are really easy to get candids from as with this one she is sooooo increadibly focused on her challenge she probably never knew you were there.<br/> <br/><b>Technical (Colour and light):</b> <br/>This is lovely .. one of the ones that does work as black and white .. but because of the subject colour would be fine as well ... as mentioned that reflection from the screen works wonders ... and the window behind hasn''t blown too much.<br/> <br/><b>To grow its vote?:</b> <br/>you played it well this time ... "oh my how cute vote" :)  The percentage you got was great due to the amount of entries ... <br/> <br/><b>Summary:</b> <br/>keep it up candids are hard and this is really good.<br/> <br/>If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via the PM system.<br/> <br/>Cheers<br/> <br/>Kari</td>', '::: Critique Club :::  Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club. First Impression - the most important one: My dad types like this .. it is cuter when this little one does it!! Composition: This is a really well balanced shot and the reflections from the screen are just magic against her face. Subject: Meets the challenge to me .. to some it doesn''t ... but kids are really easy to get candids from as with this one she is sooooo increadibly focused on her challenge she probably never knew you were there. Technical (Colour and light): This is lovely .. one of the ones that does work as black and white .. but because of the subject colour would be fine as well ... as mentioned that reflection from the screen works wonders ... and the window behind hasn''t blown too much. To grow its vote?: you played it well this time ... "oh my how cute vote" :)  The percentage you got was great due to the amount of entries ...  Summary: keep it up candids are hard and this is really good. If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via the PM system. Cheers Kari', '2006-04-24 06:17:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(2338444, 319509, 43434, '<td valign="top"><b><i>::: Critique Club :::</i></b> <br/> <br/>Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club.<br/> <br/><b>First Impression - the most important one:</b> <br/>great colours ... impressive that you got the stop motion with the waves and drips.<br/> <br/><b>Composition:</b> <br/>Not to have cropped this is great, but am unsure how you ended up with those dimensions without cropping.<br/> <br/><b>Subject:</b> <br/>Meets the challenge ... and does so well.<br/> <br/><b>Technical (Colour and light):</b> <br/>maybe a little over-saturated ... now if only you could get them to stay perfectly still .. no that wouldn''t be candid :)<br/> <br/><b>To grow its vote?:</b> <br/>Top 20 I wouldn''t complain.<br/> <br/><b>Summary:</b> <br/>Good shot ... lovely image and great capture.<br/> <br/>If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via the PM system.<br/> <br/>Cheers<br/> <br/>Kari</td>', '::: Critique Club :::  Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club. First Impression - the most important one: great colours ... impressive that you got the stop motion with the waves and drips. Composition: Not to have cropped this is great, but am unsure how you ended up with those dimensions without cropping. Subject: Meets the challenge ... and does so well. Technical (Colour and light): maybe a little over-saturated ... now if only you could get them to stay perfectly still .. no that wouldn''t be candid :) To grow its vote?: Top 20 I wouldn''t complain. Summary: Good shot ... lovely image and great capture. If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via the PM system. Cheers Kari', '2006-04-24 06:23:00.000000', NULL, 0),
