(2339847, 318095, 48570, '<td valign="top">Nice colors and expression. Beautiful portrait! Regards, B.</td>', 'Nice colors and expression. Beautiful portrait! Regards, B.', '2006-04-24 18:12:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(2340444, 319609, 52336, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from the Critique Club!</b> <br/> <br/>I think this is a wonderful example of a candid photograph with a composition that gives it an almost journalistic feel.  Lighting of the main subject is excellent, and focus is good.  Your duotone choice is the right one, and complements the warm, cozy feeling of the image perfectly.  The subject is certainly the man enjoying his paper, but in my opinion its also the large comfortable chair; lighting, texture, and composition in regard to this element is spot-on.<br/> <br/>I personally really like the composition, with the subject in the lower centre of the photograph, and all the more or less "busy" elements surrounding him.  He is a sea of calm in the midst of other activity and a jumble of other objects.<br/> <br/>Some may complain that the image lacks focus, is loose, or poorly cropped, and that the large dark area at top, with arguably disparate elements, detracts from the whole.  Whereas I think this would still be an excellent image were it more tightly cropped, I prefer the composition as-is, since, as I say, it seems to have a journalistic feeling to it.  The sum of the parts of the whole tell a story, in my view.<br/> <br/>I really enjoy this image.  C''est une très belle photo.  Félicitations!<br/> <br/>I hope this helps.<br/>Louis</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club!  I think this is a wonderful example of a candid photograph with a composition that gives it an almost journalistic feel.  Lighting of the main subject is excellent, and focus is good.  Your duotone choice is the right one, and complements the warm, cozy feeling of the image perfectly.  The subject is certainly the man enjoying his paper, but in my opinion its also the large comfortable chair; lighting, texture, and composition in regard to this element is spot-on. I personally really like the composition, with the subject in the lower centre of the photograph, and all the more or less "busy" elements surrounding him.  He is a sea of calm in the midst of other activity and a jumble of other objects. Some may complain that the image lacks focus, is loose, or poorly cropped, and that the large dark area at top, with arguably disparate elements, detracts from the whole.  Whereas I think this would still be an excellent image were it more tightly cropped, I prefer the composition as-is, since, as I say, it seems to have a journalistic feeling to it.  The sum of the parts of the whole tell a story, in my view. I really enjoy this image.  C''est une très belle photo.  Félicitations! I hope this helps.Louis', '2006-04-24 22:56:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(2340640, 319336, 42826, '<td valign="top">I thought this should ahve been in the top 10...come on voters...</td>', 'I thought this should ahve been in the top 10...come on voters...', '2006-04-25 00:06:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(2340689, 319682, 43434, '<td valign="top"><b><i>::: Critique Club :::</i></b> <br/> <br/>Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club.<br/> <br/><b>First Impression - the most important one:</b> <br/>This is lovely, it is a truely candid shot, maybe missing a little, but is still a good human study.<br/> <br/><b>Composition:</b> <br/>This is nice, but only nice, the lack of light on the childs face is an issue, but its a candid and we can not control everything.  But perhaps adding a little brightness may have helped.  The colours of her outfit really help her to stand out.  <br/> <br/><b>Subject:</b> <br/>Meets the challenge with full gusto.<br/> <br/><b>Technical (Colour and light):</b> <br/>The lighting is the issue here, but you are outside and using what nature provided ... good DOF usage, and a well cropped pic with the litttle girl on thirds.<br/> <br/><b>To grow its vote?:</b> <br/>It is not a stuning picture and you will note from the ones that won that they were.  Keep practising .. you will get there.<br/> <br/><b>Summary:</b> <br/>You have a great buildd up in your portfolio .. keep shooting.<br/> <br/>If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via the PM system.<br/> <br/>Cheers<br/> <br/>Kari</td>', '::: Critique Club :::  Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club. First Impression - the most important one: This is lovely, it is a truely candid shot, maybe missing a little, but is still a good human study. Composition: This is nice, but only nice, the lack of light on the childs face is an issue, but its a candid and we can not control everything.  But perhaps adding a little brightness may have helped.  The colours of her outfit really help her to stand out.   Subject: Meets the challenge with full gusto. Technical (Colour and light): The lighting is the issue here, but you are outside and using what nature provided ... good DOF usage, and a well cropped pic with the litttle girl on thirds. To grow its vote?: It is not a stuning picture and you will note from the ones that won that they were.  Keep practising .. you will get there. Summary: You have a great buildd up in your portfolio .. keep shooting. If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via the PM system. Cheers Kari', '2006-04-25 00:24:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(2340706, 318860, 43434, '<td valign="top"><b><i>::: Critique Club :::</i></b> <br/> <br/>Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club.<br/> <br/>Interesting to do a critique on your image but it is difficult if you don''t give us any information in your photographers comments.  When we do a critique, we go past just the photographic result, that''s what voters comments do.  The critique looks at what you were trying to achieve, how you wanted it to look and what issues you had in getting the image captured and ready for voting.<br/> <br/><b>First Impression - the most important one:</b> <br/>Ok .. black and white works ... not stunning.<br/> <br/><b>Composition:</b> <br/>This is good .. the arm of the back boy creates a leading line ... and takes the viewer to his face and expression.<br/> <br/><b>Subject:</b> <br/>Meets the challenge .. I don''t think they even knew you were in the room.<br/> <br/><b>Technical (Colour and light):</b> <br/>The black and white works here, often it is overused.  the picture is very badly out of focus .. as mentioned by most of your commentors.  This makes it difficult to give high marks and I think that this why you were marked down during the challenge.<br/> <br/><b>To grow its vote?:</b> <br/>Good sharp images score better than soft focus images.  Don''t understand why .. but that is the way that it works.<br/> <br/><b>Summary:</b> <br/>Nice shot, could do with reshooting to try and correct focus .. but as it is candid .. you just can''t do that ... keep shooting you are doing well.<br/> <br/>If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via the PM system.<br/> <br/>Cheers<br/> <br/>Kari</td>', '::: Critique Club :::  Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club. Interesting to do a critique on your image but it is difficult if you don''t give us any information in your photographers comments.  When we do a critique, we go past just the photographic result, that''s what voters comments do.  The critique looks at what you were trying to achieve, how you wanted it to look and what issues you had in getting the image captured and ready for voting. First Impression - the most important one: Ok .. black and white works ... not stunning. Composition: This is good .. the arm of the back boy creates a leading line ... and takes the viewer to his face and expression. Subject: Meets the challenge .. I don''t think they even knew you were in the room. Technical (Colour and light): The black and white works here, often it is overused.  the picture is very badly out of focus .. as mentioned by most of your commentors.  This makes it difficult to give high marks and I think that this why you were marked down during the challenge. To grow its vote?: Good sharp images score better than soft focus images.  Don''t understand why .. but that is the way that it works. Summary: Nice shot, could do with reshooting to try and correct focus .. but as it is candid .. you just can''t do that ... keep shooting you are doing well. If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via the PM system. Cheers Kari', '2006-04-25 00:30:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(2340724, 319891, 43434, '<td valign="top"><b><i>::: Critique Club :::</i></b> <br/> <br/>Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club.<br/> <br/>Interesting to do a critique on your image but it is difficult if you don''t give us any information in your photographers comments.  When we do a critique, we go past just the photographic result, that''s what voters comments do.  The critique looks at what you were trying to achieve, how you wanted it to look and what issues you had in getting the image captured and ready for voting.<br/> <br/><b>First Impression - the most important one:</b> <br/>On you little voyeur .. nice shooting.<br/> <br/><b>Composition:</b> <br/>No problems ... here .. the person in the back being out of the DOF is great and adds a secondary interest point for the eye.<br/> <br/><b>Subject:</b> <br/>Meets the challenge .. in fact you slam dunked it.<br/> <br/><b>Technical (Colour and light):</b> <br/>As mentioned by one of your commentators .. the sepia tonings work well here ... the slight flaring on the hair is lovely and keeps the picture real to me.<br/> <br/><b>To grow its vote?:</b> <br/>You came 22 .. I think that is great ... looking at those that beat ya should give you ideas at how to improve.  Taking candids is really a difficult skill and you are doing well.<br/> <br/><b>Summary:</b> <br/>Great shot .. keep it up ... I am sure many more ribbons to come.<br/> <br/>If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via the PM system.<br/> <br/>Cheers<br/> <br/>Kari</td>', '::: Critique Club :::  Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club. Interesting to do a critique on your image but it is difficult if you don''t give us any information in your photographers comments.  When we do a critique, we go past just the photographic result, that''s what voters comments do.  The critique looks at what you were trying to achieve, how you wanted it to look and what issues you had in getting the image captured and ready for voting. First Impression - the most important one: On you little voyeur .. nice shooting. Composition: No problems ... here .. the person in the back being out of the DOF is great and adds a secondary interest point for the eye. Subject: Meets the challenge .. in fact you slam dunked it. Technical (Colour and light): As mentioned by one of your commentators .. the sepia tonings work well here ... the slight flaring on the hair is lovely and keeps the picture real to me. To grow its vote?: You came 22 .. I think that is great ... looking at those that beat ya should give you ideas at how to improve.  Taking candids is really a difficult skill and you are doing well. Summary: Great shot .. keep it up ... I am sure many more ribbons to come. If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via the PM system. Cheers Kari', '2006-04-25 00:37:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(2340755, 319955, 43434, '<td valign="top"><b><i>::: Critique Club :::</i></b> <br/> <br/>Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club.<br/> <br/>I''m sorry, but without any input from you in technical details or comments, it''s just not possible to critique this image. <br/> <br/>When we do a critique, we go past just the photographic result, that''s what voters comments do.  The critique looks at what you were trying to achieve, how you wanted it to look and what issues you had in getting the image captured and ready for voting.<br/> <br/><b>First Impression - the most important one:</b> <br/>You have been bitten by the DNMC ... don''t worry .. we all get that from time to time.  I think for me the issue is more of where the focus of the picture is rather than that is a dog ... which btw is really cute and I hate dogs!<br/> <br/><b>Composition:</b> <br/>This isn''t too bad .. but here are some hints.<br/> <br/>Composition is about leading the eye into an image (painting or photo).  Research shows that the eye enters bottom left and travels up to top right ("Leading Lines Rule"). Once in there, the same research tells us that the eye finds comfort when the point of interest (POI) sits on a thirds line or intersection ("the Rule of Thirds"). <br/> <br/><b>Subject:</b> <br/>Meets the challenge .. but that is up to interpretation.  <br/> <br/><b>Technical (Colour and light):</b> <br/>I am not a huge fan of black and white .. especially of animals .. they have such wonderful colours from nature.<br/> <br/><b>To grow its vote?:</b> <br/>Think inside the very tight sqare and don''t challenge it!<br/> <br/><b>Summary:</b> <br/>You done good ... you stirred up good comment.<br/> <br/>Try staying a little safer till you build your confidence a little more .. it may help .. but then again challenge the sqaure and make it a triangle<br/> <br/>If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via the PM system.<br/> <br/>Cheers<br/> <br/>Kari</td>', '::: Critique Club :::  Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club. I''m sorry, but without any input from you in technical details or comments, it''s just not possible to critique this image.  When we do a critique, we go past just the photographic result, that''s what voters comments do.  The critique looks at what you were trying to achieve, how you wanted it to look and what issues you had in getting the image captured and ready for voting. First Impression - the most important one: You have been bitten by the DNMC ... don''t worry .. we all get that from time to time.  I think for me the issue is more of where the focus of the picture is rather than that is a dog ... which btw is really cute and I hate dogs! Composition: This isn''t too bad .. but here are some hints. Composition is about leading the eye into an image (painting or photo).  Research shows that the eye enters bottom left and travels up to top right ("Leading Lines Rule"). Once in there, the same research tells us that the eye finds comfort when the point of interest (POI) sits on a thirds line or intersection ("the Rule of Thirds").  Subject: Meets the challenge .. but that is up to interpretation.   Technical (Colour and light): I am not a huge fan of black and white .. especially of animals .. they have such wonderful colours from nature. To grow its vote?: Think inside the very tight sqare and don''t challenge it! Summary: You done good ... you stirred up good comment. Try staying a little safer till you build your confidence a little more .. it may help .. but then again challenge the sqaure and make it a triangle If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via the PM system. Cheers Kari', '2006-04-25 00:45:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(2340761, 318058, 57330, '<td valign="top">this is so inspiring : O )</td>', 'this is so inspiring : O )', '2006-04-25 00:47:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(2340840, 320009, 43434, '<td valign="top"><b><i>::: Critique Club :::</i></b> <br/> <br/>Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club.<br/> <br/><b>First Impression - the most important one:</b> <br/>Ok the title don''t do it for me .. the picture has issues .. but this is a candid and meets the challenge.  <br/> <br/>A few things tend to slammed a bit here, titles that don''t work for a picture and are required to understand the story.  A picture should in general be able to stand on its own with a title to enhance it ... this title may have confused people. <br/> <br/><b>Composition:</b> <br/>ok this is interesting ... <br/> <br/>The two metal things in the front are really badly distracting ... using them instead to assist in cropping the image .. e.g. to the corners of the picture may have assisted.<br/> <br/>when taking a shot think about the following:<br/> <br/>Composition is about leading the eye into an image (painting or photo).  Research shows that the eye enters bottom left and travels up to top right ("Leading Lines Rule"). Once in there, the same research tells us that the eye finds comfort when the point of interest (POI) sits on a thirds line or intersection ("the Rule of Thirds"). <br/> <br/>When cropping take this into account again .. as it will help. <br/> <br/><b>Subject:</b> <br/>Meets the challenge.<br/> <br/><b>Technical (Colour and light):</b> <br/>This is where you have problems ... drummers move hence motion blur which is fine .. but a higher shutter speed may have stopped the motion better ... its a candid so you are limited in what you can do really.<br/> <br/>The colour is a little off ... not sure how to fix ... but trying and playing with it may help.<br/> <br/><b>To grow its vote?:</b> <br/>Did you use a tripod?  This would help eliminate the shakes and only leave the real motion blur.  also think hard about composition as you are taking your shot - I find this helps heaps.<br/> <br/><b>Summary:</b> <br/>Interesting shot .. don''t scare people with titles too much ... you can share your faith without scaring people :)<br/> <br/>Keep it up .. you will improve .. take the time to look at others works .. so you can see what make a good pic.<br/> <br/>If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via the PM system.<br/> <br/>Cheers<br/> <br/>Kari</td>', '::: Critique Club :::  Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club. First Impression - the most important one: Ok the title don''t do it for me .. the picture has issues .. but this is a candid and meets the challenge.   A few things tend to slammed a bit here, titles that don''t work for a picture and are required to understand the story.  A picture should in general be able to stand on its own with a title to enhance it ... this title may have confused people.  Composition: ok this is interesting ...  The two metal things in the front are really badly distracting ... using them instead to assist in cropping the image .. e.g. to the corners of the picture may have assisted. when taking a shot think about the following: Composition is about leading the eye into an image (painting or photo).  Research shows that the eye enters bottom left and travels up to top right ("Leading Lines Rule"). Once in there, the same research tells us that the eye finds comfort when the point of interest (POI) sits on a thirds line or intersection ("the Rule of Thirds").  When cropping take this into account again .. as it will help.  Subject: Meets the challenge. Technical (Colour and light): This is where you have problems ... drummers move hence motion blur which is fine .. but a higher shutter speed may have stopped the motion better ... its a candid so you are limited in what you can do really. The colour is a little off ... not sure how to fix ... but trying and playing with it may help. To grow its vote?: Did you use a tripod?  This would help eliminate the shakes and only leave the real motion blur.  also think hard about composition as you are taking your shot - I find this helps heaps. Summary: Interesting shot .. don''t scare people with titles too much ... you can share your faith without scaring people :) Keep it up .. you will improve .. take the time to look at others works .. so you can see what make a good pic. If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via the PM system. Cheers Kari', '2006-04-25 01:02:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(2340852, 318848, 43434, '<td valign="top"><b><i>::: Critique Club :::</i></b> <br/> <br/>Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club.<br/> <br/><b>First Impression - the most important one:</b> <br/>If onyl we all had some interesting subject matters ... and what makes it truely candid is that you didn''t know you were going to take this shot.<br/> <br/><b>Composition:</b> <br/>It works .. I don''t really know why .. to my eye half the rules are broken... but they should be anyway.<br/> <br/><b>Subject:</b> <br/>Meets the challenge and does so in a incredible manner.<br/> <br/><b>Technical (Colour and light):</b> <br/>This is a lovely image, I personally find it a little wishy washy with the colours, but as with what he is doing this does suit.  It is sharp enough ... and I think gives a real feel for the gritty old bugger he is.<br/> <br/><b>To grow its vote?:</b> <br/>Try with another ISO setting and see that you did good this time.  Not one of your top scorers but still a lovely human element here.<br/> <br/><b>Summary:</b> <br/>Love it ... I like the energy and from the comments I have seen I like the different emotions it plays.  Congrats on achieving that.<br/> <br/>If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via the PM system.<br/> <br/>Cheers<br/> <br/>Kari</td>', '::: Critique Club :::  Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club. First Impression - the most important one: If onyl we all had some interesting subject matters ... and what makes it truely candid is that you didn''t know you were going to take this shot. Composition: It works .. I don''t really know why .. to my eye half the rules are broken... but they should be anyway. Subject: Meets the challenge and does so in a incredible manner. Technical (Colour and light): This is a lovely image, I personally find it a little wishy washy with the colours, but as with what he is doing this does suit.  It is sharp enough ... and I think gives a real feel for the gritty old bugger he is. To grow its vote?: Try with another ISO setting and see that you did good this time.  Not one of your top scorers but still a lovely human element here. Summary: Love it ... I like the energy and from the comments I have seen I like the different emotions it plays.  Congrats on achieving that. If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via the PM system. Cheers Kari', '2006-04-25 01:12:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(2340867, 318733, 43434, '<td valign="top"><b><i>::: Critique Club :::</i></b> <br/> <br/>Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club.<br/> <br/>Interesting to do a critique on your image but it is difficult if you don''t give us any information in your photographers comments.  When we do a critique, we go past just the photographic result, that''s what voters comments do.  The critique looks at what you were trying to achieve, how you wanted it to look and what issues you had in getting the image captured and ready for voting.<br/> <br/><b>First Impression - the most important one:</b> <br/>I think she got the cute vote in screeds.  Great top 50 entry for this difficult challenges.<br/> <br/><b>Composition:</b> <br/>I didn''t notice the other person till I read the comments ... I have no idea how I missed him .. must by the excellent DOF (hehe).<br/> <br/>Her face is really very centred in the picture .. and you could try other crops that may have helped with removing this ... either cropping the pic more on the left removing the boy and leaving more on the right. Problem with my comments is that I have to guess what you have done as you have not included comments.<br/> <br/><b>Subject:</b> <br/>Really meets the challenge in the most lovely way.<br/> <br/><b>Technical (Colour and light):</b> <br/>I love the colours in this shot, the DOF is really good and the sharpness is lovely.<br/> <br/><b>To grow its vote?:</b> <br/>Try recropping without the spare head ... look at the rule of thirds .. notwithstanding every other rule .. there are so many ... but this is great and as your highest scoring I hope you had a bloody nice drink after the voting finished.<br/> <br/><b>Summary:</b> <br/>Well done ... this is a shot to be truely proud of.<br/> <br/>If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via the PM system.<br/> <br/>Cheers<br/> <br/>Kari</td>', '::: Critique Club :::  Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club. Interesting to do a critique on your image but it is difficult if you don''t give us any information in your photographers comments.  When we do a critique, we go past just the photographic result, that''s what voters comments do.  The critique looks at what you were trying to achieve, how you wanted it to look and what issues you had in getting the image captured and ready for voting. First Impression - the most important one: I think she got the cute vote in screeds.  Great top 50 entry for this difficult challenges. Composition: I didn''t notice the other person till I read the comments ... I have no idea how I missed him .. must by the excellent DOF (hehe). Her face is really very centred in the picture .. and you could try other crops that may have helped with removing this ... either cropping the pic more on the left removing the boy and leaving more on the right. Problem with my comments is that I have to guess what you have done as you have not included comments. Subject: Really meets the challenge in the most lovely way. Technical (Colour and light): I love the colours in this shot, the DOF is really good and the sharpness is lovely. To grow its vote?: Try recropping without the spare head ... look at the rule of thirds .. notwithstanding every other rule .. there are so many ... but this is great and as your highest scoring I hope you had a bloody nice drink after the voting finished. Summary: Well done ... this is a shot to be truely proud of. If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via the PM system. Cheers Kari', '2006-04-25 01:18:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(2340883, 319690, 43434, '<td valign="top"><b><i>::: Critique Club :::</i></b> <br/> <br/>Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club.<br/> <br/><b>First Impression - the most important one:</b> <br/>Photojornalism here I come .. what a bugger with this weeks challenge this would have been up there.  <br/> <br/><b>Composition:</b> <br/>I think this works well ... the crop words .. and the waters tells all the story you need.<br/> <br/><b>Subject:</b> <br/>Meets the challenge .. although is he aware of you taking the picture .. it is one of those images where I think he looked at you at the wrong moment :)<br/> <br/><b>Technical (Colour and light):</b> <br/>a little wishy washy, but hey its a flood .. what else would it be.<br/> <br/><b>To grow its vote?:</b> <br/>Focus more on the man than the scene .. you will see from the top ten only in a couple did the scene have anything to add.<br/> <br/><b>Summary:</b> <br/>This is good .. I hope your home wasn''t involved.<br/> <br/>If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via the PM system.<br/> <br/>Cheers<br/> <br/>Kari</td>', '::: Critique Club :::  Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club. First Impression - the most important one: Photojornalism here I come .. what a bugger with this weeks challenge this would have been up there.   Composition: I think this works well ... the crop words .. and the waters tells all the story you need. Subject: Meets the challenge .. although is he aware of you taking the picture .. it is one of those images where I think he looked at you at the wrong moment :) Technical (Colour and light): a little wishy washy, but hey its a flood .. what else would it be. To grow its vote?: Focus more on the man than the scene .. you will see from the top ten only in a couple did the scene have anything to add. Summary: This is good .. I hope your home wasn''t involved. If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via the PM system. Cheers Kari', '2006-04-25 01:31:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(2340893, 319664, 43434, '<td valign="top"><b><i>::: Critique Club :::</i></b> <br/> <br/>Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club.<br/> <br/>Interesting to do a critique on your image but it is difficult if you don''t give us any information in your photographers comments.  When we do a critique, we go past just the photographic result, that''s what voters comments do.  The critique looks at what you were trying to achieve, how you wanted it to look and what issues you had in getting the image captured and ready for voting.<br/> <br/><b>First Impression - the most important one:</b> <br/>First up ...not bad .. I think you scored better than I did with my first!<br/> <br/><b>Composition:</b> <br/>The composition you have is fine .. but it doesn''t take advantage of the cadid of the people ... here are some addional hints for composition in future:<br/> <br/>Composition is about leading the eye into an image (painting or photo).  Research shows that the eye enters bottom left and travels up to top right ("Leading Lines Rule"). Once in there, the same research tells us that the eye finds comfort when the point of interest (POI) sits on a thirds line or intersection ("the Rule of Thirds"). <br/> <br/><b>Subject:</b> <br/>Doesn''t truely meet the challenge ... as it is about the camera and not the candid.<br/> <br/><b>Technical (Colour and light):</b> <br/>The sepia tonings work ... but be careful not to overuse them.  <br/> <br/><b>To grow its vote?:</b> <br/>Think about what the challenge is .. look at the description, if there is one, and think about what you need to make the shot.  For a candid it is hard .. cos you can''t set up and control the shot ... but for others I think you will be fine.<br/> <br/><b>Summary:</b> <br/>Good shot .. keep it up .. I want to see more from you.<br/> <br/>If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via the PM system.<br/> <br/>Cheers<br/> <br/>Kari</td>', '::: Critique Club :::  Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club. Interesting to do a critique on your image but it is difficult if you don''t give us any information in your photographers comments.  When we do a critique, we go past just the photographic result, that''s what voters comments do.  The critique looks at what you were trying to achieve, how you wanted it to look and what issues you had in getting the image captured and ready for voting. First Impression - the most important one: First up ...not bad .. I think you scored better than I did with my first! Composition: The composition you have is fine .. but it doesn''t take advantage of the cadid of the people ... here are some addional hints for composition in future: Composition is about leading the eye into an image (painting or photo).  Research shows that the eye enters bottom left and travels up to top right ("Leading Lines Rule"). Once in there, the same research tells us that the eye finds comfort when the point of interest (POI) sits on a thirds line or intersection ("the Rule of Thirds").  Subject: Doesn''t truely meet the challenge ... as it is about the camera and not the candid. Technical (Colour and light): The sepia tonings work ... but be careful not to overuse them.   To grow its vote?: Think about what the challenge is .. look at the description, if there is one, and think about what you need to make the shot.  For a candid it is hard .. cos you can''t set up and control the shot ... but for others I think you will be fine. Summary: Good shot .. keep it up .. I want to see more from you. If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via the PM system. Cheers Kari', '2006-04-25 01:36:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(2340897, 318501, 54770, '<td valign="top">Never has a picture made me cry as much as this one. I love it. If there ever was a picture that could tell a story this one is it.</td>', 'Never has a picture made me cry as much as this one. I love it. If there ever was a picture that could tell a story this one is it.', '2006-04-25 01:38:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(2340901, 317446, 43434, '<td valign="top"><b><i>::: Critique Club :::</i></b> <br/> <br/>Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club.<br/> <br/><b>First Impression - the most important one:</b> <br/>An emotionally drawing image.<br/> <br/><b>Composition:</b> <br/>I think this works ok .. as the lines in the picture draw your eye towards the top right courner.<br/> <br/><b>Subject:</b> <br/>Meets the challenge .. is a scary way.<br/> <br/><b>Technical (Colour and light):</b> <br/>Black and white works well for this ... it appears shartp ... a little less DOF may have helped but I am not sure.<br/> <br/><b>To grow its vote?:</b> <br/>a head or face maybe ... knowing that he was alive ... for a first entry you have done really really well.<br/> <br/><b>Summary:</b> <br/>Good shooting ... I can see that you are going to create some stirs around here with good hard placed emotional shots like this one.<br/> <br/>If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via the PM system.<br/> <br/>Cheers<br/> <br/>Kari</td>', '::: Critique Club :::  Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club. First Impression - the most important one: An emotionally drawing image. Composition: I think this works ok .. as the lines in the picture draw your eye towards the top right courner. Subject: Meets the challenge .. is a scary way. Technical (Colour and light): Black and white works well for this ... it appears shartp ... a little less DOF may have helped but I am not sure. To grow its vote?: a head or face maybe ... knowing that he was alive ... for a first entry you have done really really well. Summary: Good shooting ... I can see that you are going to create some stirs around here with good hard placed emotional shots like this one. If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via the PM system. Cheers Kari', '2006-04-25 01:40:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(2341004, 319656, 43434, '<td valign="top"><b><i>::: Critique Club :::</i></b> <br/> <br/>Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club.<br/> <br/><b>First Impression - the most important one:</b> <br/>Such a cute kid ... and such a shove off look .. there is everything candid in that look.<br/> <br/><b>Composition:</b> <br/>The top of the head missing is an issue ... the image is slightly soft .. but that is not a major ... <br/> <br/><b>Subject:</b> <br/>Definately meets the challenge .. although I think that many didn''t think so hence the voting.<br/> <br/><b>Technical (Colour and light):</b> <br/>Lovely natural light and good pastel colours.<br/> <br/><b>To grow its vote?:</b> <br/>Pays to get the whole body if you can ... hard to dictate for a candid .. but sometimes we get a candid and others don''t think it is real .. there is little ways around this.<br/> <br/><b>Summary:</b> <br/>Good shot .. keep it up you are improving all the time.<br/> <br/>If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via the PM system.<br/> <br/>Cheers<br/> <br/>Kari</td>', '::: Critique Club :::  Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club. First Impression - the most important one: Such a cute kid ... and such a shove off look .. there is everything candid in that look. Composition: The top of the head missing is an issue ... the image is slightly soft .. but that is not a major ...  Subject: Definately meets the challenge .. although I think that many didn''t think so hence the voting. Technical (Colour and light): Lovely natural light and good pastel colours. To grow its vote?: Pays to get the whole body if you can ... hard to dictate for a candid .. but sometimes we get a candid and others don''t think it is real .. there is little ways around this. Summary: Good shot .. keep it up you are improving all the time. If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via the PM system. Cheers Kari', '2006-04-25 03:03:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(2341011, 318972, 43434, '<td valign="top"><b><i>::: Critique Club :::</i></b> <br/> <br/>Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club.<br/> <br/><b>First Impression - the most important one:</b> <br/>Is this kid lost or what ... <br/> <br/><b>Composition:</b> <br/>Lovely .. the DOF is great ... my only issue would be that he is entirely centred.<br/> <br/><b>Subject:</b> <br/>meets the challenge with gusto.<br/> <br/><b>Technical (Colour and light):</b> <br/>With that hat I would expect a darker face . .that it isn''t is a testament to your shooting ... I like the lighting and how this is just a flukey type shot.<br/> <br/><b>To grow its vote?:</b> <br/>Shoot the detractors .. this deservered better but only those who can read the voters minds do extremely well.<br/> <br/><b>Summary:</b> <br/>Cool candid .. well done.<br/> <br/>If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via the PM system.<br/> <br/>Cheers<br/> <br/>Kari</td>', '::: Critique Club :::  Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club. First Impression - the most important one: Is this kid lost or what ...  Composition: Lovely .. the DOF is great ... my only issue would be that he is entirely centred. Subject: meets the challenge with gusto. Technical (Colour and light): With that hat I would expect a darker face . .that it isn''t is a testament to your shooting ... I like the lighting and how this is just a flukey type shot. To grow its vote?: Shoot the detractors .. this deservered better but only those who can read the voters minds do extremely well. Summary: Cool candid .. well done. If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via the PM system. Cheers Kari', '2006-04-25 03:08:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(2341019, 318807, 43434, '<td valign="top"><b><i>::: Critique Club :::</i></b> <br/> <br/>Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club.<br/> <br/><b>First Impression - the most important one:</b> <br/>Nice sharing shot.  Good candid ... lovely couple.<br/> <br/><b>Composition:</b> <br/>This is well done, the picture is nicely cropped ... <br/> <br/><b>Subject:</b> <br/>meets the challenge.<br/> <br/><b>Technical (Colour and light):</b> <br/>Pity we can''t direct the sun as a light source it would have been so much more helpful.  This is crisp and lovely shot.<br/> <br/><b>To grow its vote?:</b> <br/>This is a good solid shot as shown from the voting.<br/> <br/><b>Summary:</b> <br/>Good work .. can''t wait to see more.<br/> <br/>If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via the PM system.<br/> <br/>Cheers<br/> <br/>Kari</td>', '::: Critique Club :::  Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club. First Impression - the most important one: Nice sharing shot.  Good candid ... lovely couple. Composition: This is well done, the picture is nicely cropped ...  Subject: meets the challenge. Technical (Colour and light): Pity we can''t direct the sun as a light source it would have been so much more helpful.  This is crisp and lovely shot. To grow its vote?: This is a good solid shot as shown from the voting. Summary: Good work .. can''t wait to see more. If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via the PM system. Cheers Kari', '2006-04-25 03:17:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(2341025, 318628, 43434, '<td valign="top"><b><i>::: Critique Club :::</i></b> <br/> <br/>Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club.<br/> <br/><b>First Impression - the most important one:</b> <br/>Makes me wonder about the places this photographer hangs out ... what a great capture.<br/> <br/><b>Composition:</b> <br/>The crop may be the issue ... but this may be all you had to work with .. your commentators have mentioned several improvements .. try them out and see how that goes.<br/> <br/><b>Subject:</b> <br/>Meets the challenge well ...<br/> <br/><b>Technical (Colour and light):</b> <br/>She is not as sharp as him .. but then again .. what you gonna do go up and say hold still so I can take this picture .. you did good with what you got ... <br/> <br/><b>To grow its vote?:</b> <br/>Add a little brightness play a little more with contrast ... and just keep learning from each thing you do ... that is the best way to learn.<br/> <br/><b>Summary:</b> <br/>Good luck good shooting .. and keep it up.<br/> <br/>If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via the PM system.<br/> <br/>Cheers<br/> <br/>Kari</td>', '::: Critique Club :::  Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club. First Impression - the most important one: Makes me wonder about the places this photographer hangs out ... what a great capture. Composition: The crop may be the issue ... but this may be all you had to work with .. your commentators have mentioned several improvements .. try them out and see how that goes. Subject: Meets the challenge well ... Technical (Colour and light): She is not as sharp as him .. but then again .. what you gonna do go up and say hold still so I can take this picture .. you did good with what you got ...  To grow its vote?: Add a little brightness play a little more with contrast ... and just keep learning from each thing you do ... that is the best way to learn. Summary: Good luck good shooting .. and keep it up. If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via the PM system. Cheers Kari', '2006-04-25 03:21:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(2341185, 318637, 42070, '<td valign="top">I love the picture. But makes me ask a question that has been bugging me for a long time. When shooting such a picture, do I need a permission of whom I''m shooting? And if not, then is it really okay to publish it like this without their knowledge?<br/>Thanks. <br/></td>', 'I love the picture. But makes me ask a question that has been bugging me for a long time. When shooting such a picture, do I need a permission of whom I''m shooting? And if not, then is it really okay to publish it like this without their knowledge?Thanks. ', '2006-04-25 06:08:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(2341476, 318637, 15711, '<td valign="top">top ten - Great job.  I had it scored pretty high. The colors, and the stop action is enhanced by the story it tells.  Congrats.</td>', 'top ten - Great job.  I had it scored pretty high. The colors, and the stop action is enhanced by the story it tells.  Congrats.', '2006-04-25 09:33:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(2341523, 317626, 13759, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by GoodEnd:</b></div><hr/><i> You do what you think right! To me it´s wrong, but you´re free. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Sorry if you felt my coment rude in some aspect or "Judgemental", as you say. I only refer to the kind of picture and the challenge theme. I just think like many others does: that a candid needs a person or a live creature.<br/>I believe the same thing as you. That God will judge and give to each one what he deserves. To those believe in His son the great award, the ethernal life.<br/>I´m sorry by your feeling about my coment and hope you can forgiven me.<br/>Peace and rest for you in Jesus name.</td>', 'Originally posted by GoodEnd: You do what you think right! To me it´s wrong, but you´re free.  Sorry if you felt my coment rude in some aspect or "Judgemental", as you say. I only refer to the kind of picture and the challenge theme. I just think like many others does: that a candid needs a person or a live creature.I believe the same thing as you. That God will judge and give to each one what he deserves. To those believe in His son the great award, the ethernal life.I´m sorry by your feeling about my coment and hope you can forgiven me.Peace and rest for you in Jesus name.', '2006-04-25 09:45:57.000000', NULL, 0),
