(2342122, 318568, 32321, '<td valign="top">Hi! Heres a comment from the Critique Club.<br/> <br/>First Impression:<br/>Nice leading lines/vanishing point. My eyes follow the lines and then back to the person on the right. Dont see anything candid!<br/> <br/>Composition:<br/>Very nice lines. Dark panels in the ceiling really work well with the walls and the rest of the ceiling. The curved walls really add to the perspective. Nice to see the vanishing point off of center. Motion blur works well in setting the mood.<br/> <br/>Subject:<br/>Not sure it meets the challenge. Candid implies catching peoples expression when they dont expect it. Cant see any ones expression.<br/> <br/>Technical:<br/>You didnt include any processing information so I dont know what your camera settings were or what you were trying to achieve. B&amp;W works well. Focus is a little soft.  Some USM may have helped too.<br/> <br/>Suggestions:<br/>Camera settings, can usually be found by using your viewer and right clicking, and selecting properties. You may have to make another selection based on your viewer. As long as its an original file, the camera data should be there.<br/> <br/>Summary:<br/>Congratulations on your best score.  You have a good eye. Keep shooting!<br/></td>', 'Hi! Heres a comment from the Critique Club. First Impression:Nice leading lines/vanishing point. My eyes follow the lines and then back to the person on the right. Dont see anything candid! Composition:Very nice lines. Dark panels in the ceiling really work well with the walls and the rest of the ceiling. The curved walls really add to the perspective. Nice to see the vanishing point off of center. Motion blur works well in setting the mood. Subject:Not sure it meets the challenge. Candid implies catching peoples expression when they dont expect it. Cant see any ones expression. Technical:You didnt include any processing information so I dont know what your camera settings were or what you were trying to achieve. B&W works well. Focus is a little soft.  Some USM may have helped too. Suggestions:Camera settings, can usually be found by using your viewer and right clicking, and selecting properties. You may have to make another selection based on your viewer. As long as its an original file, the camera data should be there. Summary:Congratulations on your best score.  You have a good eye. Keep shooting!', '2006-04-25 13:18:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(2342186, 318058, 57392, '<td valign="top">Great Photo Well done</td>', 'Great Photo Well done', '2006-04-25 13:45:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(2343038, 319760, 55952, '<td valign="top">Wow, this is a remarkable photograph. I did not have a chance to vote on this one, but this would have been my first pick. The description sums it all up, and really sends shivers down my spine. I feel bad for the man. Both men. Fantastic job, congratulations.</td>', 'Wow, this is a remarkable photograph. I did not have a chance to vote on this one, but this would have been my first pick. The description sums it all up, and really sends shivers down my spine. I feel bad for the man. Both men. Fantastic job, congratulations.', '2006-04-25 19:37:23.000000', NULL, 0),
